'use strict';
(() => {
const D=globalThis.RA.D;
const C=(senseId,domain,en,zh,structure,grammar,rationale)=>({senseId,domain,en,zh,structure,grammar,rationale,sourceType:'authored'});
const M=(wrong,right,reason,errorType='meaning')=>({wrong,right,reason,errorType});
const Q=(s,prompt,answer,wrong1,wrong2,explain,errorType='meaning')=>({s,prompt,answer,wrong1,wrong2,explain,errorType});
const E=(origin,w)=>({origin,prefix:null,root:null,suffix:null,source:`Etymonline: https://www.etymonline.com/word/${w.toLowerCase().replaceAll(' ','-')}`});
const P=(w,origin,contexts,mistake,qs)=>D(w,{etymology:E(origin,w),contexts:Array.isArray(contexts)?contexts:[contexts],mistakes:[mistake],quiz:qs.map((q,i)=>({id:`${w}.q${i+1}`,senseId:`${w}.s${q.s}`,prompt:q.prompt,answer:q.answer,options:[q.answer,q.wrong1,q.wrong2],explain:q.explain,errorType:q.errorType,type:'辨义与用法'}))});
P('repot','From re- “again” + pot; repot means move a plant into a larger or fresh pot with new soil.',C('repot.s1','园艺','The gardener repotted the basil when its roots began to fill the small container.','罗勒的根系快要长满小盆时，园丁给它换了一个盆。','repot a plant into + pot','动词：把植物移入新盆，通常换用新土或更大的容器。','roots need more space.','园艺'),M('She repotted the basil by leaving it in the same pot and adding no soil or space.','She repotted the basil by moving it into a larger pot with fresh soil.','留在原盆里没有移盆，不是 repot。','meaning'),[Q(1,'Why did the gardener repot the basil?','Its roots needed more room.','Its leaves needed to be printed again.','It was a reptile.','Repot means move a plant to a different pot, often a larger one.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','repot a crowded houseplant','repot a houseplant into a calendar','repot the soil away from a plant','The plant is moved into a pot with more growing room.','collocation'),Q(1,'A plant has outgrown its container, so the owner transfers it to another one. The owner…','repots the plant','reproaches the plant','reprocesses the plant','Moving it to a new pot is repotting.','context'),Q(1,'What does re- mean in repot?','again or anew','not','under','The plant is potted again in a new container.','word-formation')]);
P('represent','From Old French representer, from Latin repraesentare “make present”; represent means act for someone, stand for an idea, or describe something in a particular way.',[C('represent.s1','通用','Two elected delegates represent the village at the regional meeting.','两名民选代表在地区会议上代表该村。','represent a person/group at + event','动词：代表某人或团体发言、行事。','delegates speak for village.','通用'),C('represent.s2','通用','In this diagram, the blue arrows represent the movement of warm air.','在这张图中，蓝色箭头表示暖空气的流动。','represent an idea/value/quantity','动词：作为某概念或数量的象征、标志。','arrows symbolize air flow.','通用'),C('represent.s3','书面','The advertisement represented the medicine as a guaranteed cure, although the evidence was weak.','尽管证据薄弱，广告仍把这种药描绘成有保证的疗法。','represent someone/something as + description','动词：把人或事描述成某种样子，有时不准确。','advertisement makes a claim.','书面')],M('The blue arrows represent warm air, but the caption says they stand for cold water.','The blue arrows represent warm air, as the caption explains.','同一图例把蓝箭头解释为冷水，与其所代表的暖空气冲突。','meaning'),[Q(1,'The delegates represent their village at the meeting. They…','speak or act for the village','describe the village as a medicine','move the village into a larger pot','Sense 1 is to act on behalf of a person or group.','meaning'),Q(2,'In a chart, a blue line may represent rainfall. It…','stands for rainfall','acts as an elected delegate','reprints the rainfall','Sense 2 is symbolic representation.','context'),Q(3,'An ad represents a product as safe. The ad…','describes the product in that way','formally reprimands it','moves it to a new location','Sense 3 concerns how something is portrayed or characterized.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which construction is correct?','represent the team at the meeting','represent at the meeting the team to','represent the team as at meeting for','Represent can take the group and then a phrase naming the event.','grammar')]);
P('representation','From represent + -ation, from Latin repraesentare “make present”; representation is the right to act for someone, a depiction, or a formal complaint or opinion.',[C('representation.s1','职业','The tenants elected a lawyer to provide representation during the negotiations.','租户选出一名律师，在谈判中为他们提供代理。','legal/elected representation; representation for + group','名词：代表某人发言或行事的资格、权利或行为。','lawyer acts on tenants’ behalf.','法律'),C('representation.s2','通用','The map is a simple representation of the valley’s rivers and roads.','这张地图是对山谷中河流和道路的简明呈现。','a representation of + object/idea','名词：显示、描绘事物的图像、描述或符号。','map depicts geography.','通用'),C('representation.s3','正式','The residents made a formal representation to the council about the unsafe crossing.','居民就这处不安全的过街设施向委员会作了正式陈述。','make a representation to + authority','名词：向机构提出的正式意见、陈述或交涉。','residents submit complaint.','正式')],M('The map is a representation of the valley, but it deliberately shows no rivers, roads, or other features of it.','The map is a representation of the valley because it depicts its rivers and roads.','完全没有描绘山谷特征的图不能充分呈现该山谷。','meaning'),[Q(1,'A lawyer provides representation for tenants. The lawyer…','acts or speaks on their behalf','draws a map of their building only','reprints their lease','Sense 1 is representation as advocacy or agency.','meaning'),Q(2,'A map is a representation of a valley because it…','depicts the valley’s features','is a formal complaint to the council','is a person elected to speak','Sense 2 is a depiction or model.','context'),Q(3,'Residents make a representation to the council when they…','submit a formal statement or complaint','draw the council as a river','repress the crossing','Sense 3 is a formal expression of an opinion to an authority.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','representation of the landscape','representation to the landscape of by','representative the landscape of','The noun commonly takes of before the thing depicted.','grammar')]);
P('representative','From represent + -ative, ultimately from Latin repraesentare; representative is someone chosen to speak for a group or something typical of that group.',[C('representative.s1','职业','A customer-service representative called to explain the delay in the delivery.','一名客服代表打电话解释了送货延迟的原因。','a representative of/for + organization','名词：受委托代表团体或组织发言、办事的人。','employee speaks for company.','职业'),C('representative.s2','科学','The sample included farms from each district, making it representative of the whole region.','样本涵盖了每个区的农场，因此能代表整个地区的情况。','representative of + group/population','形容词：能体现某群体总体特征的；有代表性的。','sample reflects whole region.','科学')],M('The survey used only one unusual farm but called its results representative of every farm in the region.','The survey sampled farms across all districts to make its results representative of the region.','单个异常样本不足以体现整个地区的典型情况。','meaning'),[Q(1,'A customer-service representative is…','an employee who acts for the company','a farm typical of a region','a formal complaint','Sense 1 names a person who represents an organization.','meaning'),Q(2,'A representative sample of farms…','reflects the wider group fairly well','contains only an unusual outlier','speaks officially for the farms','Sense 2 means typical enough to show what a group is like.','context'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','a representative of the company','a represent of company','representative at company from of','A representative can be followed by of to identify the organization.','grammar'),Q(1,'A sample is representative when it…','shows characteristics of the larger population','excludes almost every kind of subject','is an elected person','The adjective refers to how typical a sample is.','meaning')]);
P('repress','From Latin reprimere “press back,” from re- + premere “press”; repress means use force to put down a group, or hold back a feeling.',[C('repress.s1','政治','The government sent troops to repress the uprising in the northern district.','政府派兵镇压北部地区的起义。','repress a protest/uprising','动词：以武力压制抗议、起义或群体。','troops put down uprising.','政治'),C('repress.s2','心理','He tried to repress his anger during the meeting and waited until afterward to respond.','他在会议上努力压住怒火，等会后再回应。','repress a feeling/impulse','动词：克制、不表露某种情感或冲动。','speaker holds back anger.','心理')],M('The troops repressed the protest by organizing it freely and helping it grow.','The troops repressed the protest by forcibly stopping it.','支持示威扩大不是镇压示威。','meaning'),[Q(1,'Troops repress an uprising when they…','use force to put it down','organize it and help it spread','reprint its demands','Sense 1 means suppress a protest or group by force.','meaning'),Q(2,'To repress anger during a meeting is to…','hold back its outward expression','shout it at everyone immediately','write it on a map','Sense 2 is to control or conceal a feeling.','context'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','repress a protest','repress to protest down','repress a protest with it away','Repress directly takes the protest or uprising as its object.','grammar'),Q(1,'The root idea behind repress is to press…','back','forward again','into a new pot','Latin reprimere is formed from re- and premere, “press.”','word-formation')]);
P('repression','From repress + -ion, from Latin reprimere “press back”; repression is harsh political control or the psychological act of keeping a desire or memory outside awareness.',C('repression.s1','社会','The report documented years of political repression and restrictions on public speech.','报告记录了多年来的政治压制以及对公开言论的限制。','political/state repression','名词：以严厉手段控制人群；心理学中也指把欲望或记忆排除在意识之外。','rights are curtailed.','社会'),M('The report called the policy repression even though it expanded public speech and removed all controls.','The report called the policy repression because it used force and restrictions to silence opposition.','扩大言论自由并取消管控与压制相反。','meaning'),[Q(1,'Political repression often involves…','force and strict controls limiting opposition','free expression with no restrictions','reproduction of a political poster','Repression is harsh control of people.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','repression of public speech','repression for speak publicly','repressed public speeching','Repression commonly takes of before the activity or people controlled.','grammar'),Q(1,'A government imprisons critics and bans peaceful protests. This is…','political repression','representative government','reproductive policy','The measures forcibly limit opposition.','context'),Q(1,'Repression is the noun related to…','repress','represent','require','Repression is formed from the verb repress.','word-formation')]);
P('repressive','From repress + -ive, based on Latin reprimere “press back”; repressive describes forceful control that restricts opposition or free expression.',C('repressive.s1','政治','The repressive law banned peaceful meetings and punished newspapers that criticized officials.','这项压制性法律禁止和平集会，并惩罚批评官员的报纸。','repressive government/law/regime','形容词：使用武力或严苛规则阻止反对意见或自由表达。','law restricts speech.','政治'),M('The repressive law protected open criticism and removed every penalty for peaceful opposition.','The repressive law restricted criticism and punished peaceful opposition.','保护公开批评、取消惩罚不是压制性的表现。','meaning'),[Q(1,'A repressive law is one that…','severely restricts opposition or expression','guarantees unrestricted public debate','requires a plant to be repotted','Repressive describes harsh control.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','a repressive regime','a repressively regime','a regime repressive of to','Repressive is an adjective modifying regime.','grammar'),Q(1,'A ruler bans protests and jails peaceful critics. The rule is…','repressive','reputable','reproductive','It uses strict control to prevent opposition.','context'),Q(1,'Repressive is formed from…','repress + -ive','repression + -ed','represent + -ly','The adjective suffix -ive forms repressive from repress.','word-formation')]);
P('reprieve','From Anglo-French reprimer “take back or defer,” of uncertain deeper origin; a reprieve is an official delay or cancellation of punishment, or to grant one.',[C('reprieve.s1','法律','The governor granted the prisoner a reprieve while new evidence was reviewed.','新证据审查期间，州长暂缓了对囚犯的惩罚。','grant/receive a reprieve from + punishment','名词：官方下令推迟或取消惩罚。','sentence is postponed.','法律'),C('reprieve.s2','法律','The court reprieved the defendant until the appeal could be heard.','法院暂缓执行对被告的惩罚，等待上诉审理。','reprieve someone from + punishment','动词：推迟或取消官方处罚。','court delays punishment.','法律')],M('The governor granted a reprieve by carrying out the sentence immediately and allowing no delay.','The governor granted a reprieve by delaying the sentence while the appeal was reviewed.','立即执行且不延迟不是暂缓处罚。','meaning'),[Q(1,'A prisoner granted a reprieve receives…','an official delay or cancellation of punishment','a stricter punishment carried out at once','a new representative','A reprieve is a formal postponement or cancellation.','meaning'),Q(2,'The court reprieved the defendant until the appeal. It…','delayed the punishment','reprinted the appeal','ordered punishment to happen before review','Reprieve as a verb means postpone or cancel an official penalty.','context'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','a reprieve from the sentence','a reprieve to the sentence from of','reprieve the sentence at by delay','A reprieve from a punishment is a common construction.','grammar'),Q(1,'A reprieve is most closely related to…','a temporary delay','a reprimand','a permanent conviction','It gives a person a delay from punishment.','meaning')]);
P('reprimand','From French reprimander, from Latin reprimere “press back”; reprimand means officially tell someone they have done wrong, or a formal statement of disapproval.',[C('reprimand.s1','职业','The supervisor reprimanded the technician for bypassing the safety check.','主管因技术员跳过安全检查而正式训斥了他。','reprimand someone for + action','动词：正式告知某人其行为有错。','supervisor corrects misconduct.','职场'),C('reprimand.s2','职业','The employee received a written reprimand for repeatedly missing required inspections.','这名员工因多次漏做规定检查而收到书面申斥。','receive/issue a formal reprimand','名词：正式表达不赞成的训斥或书面警告。','written notice of disapproval.','职场')],M('The supervisor reprimanded the technician by praising him for skipping the safety check.','The supervisor reprimanded the technician for skipping the safety check.','赞扬跳过安全检查不是训斥或纠正错误。','meaning'),[Q(1,'A supervisor reprimands a worker for an unsafe act by…','officially telling the worker the act was wrong','rewarding the worker for it','reprinting the safety manual','Reprimand means formally criticize someone for misconduct.','meaning'),Q(2,'A written reprimand is…','a formal statement of disapproval','an award for excellent work','a reprieve from all workplace rules','The noun names an official warning or criticism.','context'),Q(1,'Which pattern is correct?','reprimand someone for an error','reprimand someone to an error','reprimand for someone an error','The action prompting the reprimand is introduced by for.','grammar'),Q(1,'Which is closest to reprimand?','rebuke','praise','reproduce','A reprimand is a formal rebuke.','meaning')]);
P('reprint','From re- “again” + print, from Old French preinte “impression”; reprint means produce another printed batch of a work already published.',C('reprint.s1','出版','The publisher will reprint the guide because all copies of the first edition have sold.','第一版全部售罄后，出版社将重印这本指南。','reprint a book/article; reprint an edition','动词：再次印制已出版的作品。','publisher prints another batch.','出版'),M('The publisher reprinted the guide by printing it for the very first time.','The publisher reprinted the guide after the first edition sold out.','首次印制是 print；reprint 指再次印制。','distinction'),[Q(1,'A publisher reprints a book when it…','prints another batch of an already published work','writes an entirely unrelated new book','reprimands the author','Reprint means print again.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','reprint the article in a new edition','reprint a new article for its first printing','reprint the article to a pot','A reprint is another printing of an existing work.','collocation'),Q(1,'All copies sell out, so the publisher produces more copies of the same text. The publisher…','reprints it','represses it','relegates it','The work has already been printed once.','context'),Q(1,'What does re- contribute to reprint?','again','under','against','It marks another printing.','word-formation')]);
P('reproach','From Old French reprochier “bring up as a reproach,” perhaps from Latin re- + prope “near”; reproach means blame someone with disappointment, or a blaming remark or source of shame.',[C('reproach.s1','书面','She reproached herself for forgetting to lock the laboratory door.','她因忘记锁实验室的门而自责。','reproach someone for + fault','动词：带着失望或不满责备某人。','speaker blames herself for error.','书面'),C('reproach.s2','书面','His careless comment was a reproach to the team’s careful safety record.','他粗心的评论有损团队一向严谨的安全记录。','a reproach to + person/standard; words of reproach','名词：责备的话，或使人蒙羞、与标准不符的事物。','comment damages reputation.','书面')],M('She reproached herself for the mistake by congratulating herself and insisting she had done nothing wrong.','She reproached herself for the mistake and resolved to check the door next time.','自我祝贺、否认错误与自责不符。','meaning'),[Q(1,'She reproached herself for forgetting the key. She…','blamed herself for the mistake','praised herself for remembering','reprinted the key','Reproach as a verb means blame with disapproval.','meaning'),Q(2,'A comment described as a reproach to the team…','brings shame or reflects badly on the team','is a formal representative of it','is a fresh copy of its report','Sense 2 can mean something that brings shame.','context'),Q(1,'Which phrase is correct?','reproach him for being careless','reproach him of his carelessness to','reproach for him by careless','Reproach commonly takes a person, followed by for + fault.','grammar'),Q(1,'Words of reproach express…','blame or disapproval','a reprieve from punishment','a request for a new edition','The noun may refer to words that criticize someone.','meaning')]);
P('reprocess','From re- “again” + process, from Latin processus “advance”; reprocess means treat used material again so it can be used a second time.',C('reprocess.s1','工业','The plant will reprocess the used plastic into pellets for new products.','工厂将把用过的塑料再加工成颗粒，用于制造新产品。','reprocess used/waste material into + product','动词：再次处理已经使用过的材料，使其可以再用。','waste is treated for reuse.','工业'),M('The plant reprocessed the plastic by dumping it untreated and making it unusable.','The plant reprocessed the plastic by cleaning and reshaping it for reuse.','未经处理地丢弃并使其无法使用，不是再加工。','meaning'),[Q(1,'A plant reprocesses used plastic to…','treat it again so it can be reused','discard it without treatment','reprint it as a book','Reprocess means process used material again.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','reprocess waste into usable material','reprocess waste out of any reuse','reprocess to waste material in','The material is treated again to produce something usable.','grammar'),Q(1,'Used metal is cleaned and melted to make new parts. It is…','reprocessed','reproached','repressed','The metal is treated again for another use.','context'),Q(1,'What does re- mean in reprocess?','again','without','between','It signals that the process is done another time.','word-formation')]);
P('reproduce','From Latin reproducere “produce again,” from re- + producere “bring forth”; reproduce means make a copy, produce offspring, or cause a result to happen again.',[C('reproduce.s1','通用','The scanner can reproduce the faded map without losing its small labels.','这台扫描仪可以复制这幅褪色的地图，同时保留细小标注。','reproduce a picture/document/sound','动词：制作图像、声音或文件的复制品。','scanner makes a copy.','通用'),C('reproduce.s2','生物','Sea turtles reproduce by laying eggs on sandy beaches.','海龟通过在沙滩上产卵繁殖。','reproduce by + -ing; reproduce offspring','动词：产生后代。','animals produce young.','生物'),C('reproduce.s3','科学','The lab repeated the experiment but could not reproduce the original result.','实验室重复了实验，却无法重现最初的结果。','reproduce a result/effect','动词：使结果或情形再次发生。','researchers repeat test.','科学')],M('The scanner reproduced the map by changing every label and omitting the original markings.','The scanner reproduced the map by making a copy that preserved its labels and markings.','改变并遗漏原有内容不能算准确复制该地图。','meaning'),[Q(1,'A scanner reproduces a map when it…','makes a copy of it','produces young turtles','causes an experiment to fail','Sense 1 is making a copy.','meaning'),Q(2,'Sea turtles reproduce by laying eggs. They…','produce offspring','make copies of maps','repeat an experiment’s result','Sense 2 refers to biological reproduction.','context'),Q(3,'Researchers reproduce an experimental result when they…','make the same result happen again under a test','print a map for the first time','repress a political group','Sense 3 concerns repeating an outcome.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','reproduce the image accurately','reproduce to the image by','reproducingly the image out','Reproduce takes the copied image as a direct object.','grammar')]);
P('reproduction','From reproduce + -ion, from Latin reproducere “produce again”; reproduction is a copy, the biological process of producing young, or the replay of sound or images.',[C('reproduction.s1','通用','The gallery sells a high-quality reproduction of the nineteenth-century painting.','美术馆出售这幅十九世纪画作的高质量复制品。','a reproduction of + artwork/object','名词：画作或物品的复制品。','gallery offers a copy.','艺术'),C('reproduction.s2','生物','The documentary explains how reproduction differs among flowering plants.','这部纪录片讲解了开花植物之间的繁殖方式有何不同。','sexual/asexual reproduction','名词：植物或动物产生后代的过程。','program discusses offspring.','生物'),C('reproduction.s3','媒体','The speakers provide clear reproduction of voices recorded in the hall.','扬声器能够清晰重现录制于大厅中的人声。','sound/image reproduction','名词：声音或图像再次播放、呈现的过程。','speakers replay voices.','媒体')],M('The gallery labeled the original painting itself a reproduction even though no copy had been made.','The gallery labeled the printed copy a reproduction of the original painting.','原画本身不是它自己的复制品。','meaning'),[Q(1,'A reproduction of a painting is…','a copy of the painting','the artist’s biological offspring','a new political restriction','Sense 1 means a copied object.','meaning'),Q(2,'Biological reproduction is the process by which organisms…','produce offspring','make painted copies','replay recorded sound','Sense 2 concerns producing young.','context'),Q(3,'Sound reproduction refers to…','playing recorded sound again','breeding an animal','making an official complaint','Sense 3 is the playback of audio.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which phrase is correct?','a reproduction of the sculpture','a reproduce of the sculpture','reproduction to sculpture into','The noun commonly takes of before the copied item.','grammar')]);
P('reproductive','From reproduce + -ive, from Latin reproducere “produce again”; reproductive describes the biological process of producing offspring.',C('reproductive.s1','生物','The clinic offers counseling about reproductive health and family planning.','这家诊所提供有关生殖健康和计划生育的咨询。','reproductive health/system/cycle','形容词：与生物产生后代的过程有关。','counseling concerns fertility and health.','生物'),M('The clinic’s reproductive services were unrelated to fertility, pregnancy, or the production of offspring.','The clinic’s reproductive services included fertility counseling and prenatal care.','与生育或繁殖完全无关的服务不属于 reproductive 范畴。','meaning'),[Q(1,'Reproductive health concerns…','the body and processes involved in producing offspring','the reprinting of a book','political representation','Reproductive is related to biological reproduction.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','the reproductive system','the reproduction systemical','reproductive of system to','Reproductive is an adjective modifying system.','grammar'),Q(1,'A study examines how animals produce young. It studies…','reproductive behavior','representative speech','residual material','Producing offspring is a reproductive process.','context'),Q(1,'Reproductive is derived from which verb?','reproduce','reprove','repress','It is formed from reproduce with the adjective suffix -ive.','word-formation')]);
P('reprove','From Old French reprover, from Latin reprobare “disapprove”; reprove means criticize someone’s fault with seriousness and disapproval.',C('reprove.s1','书面','The coach reproved the players for ignoring the agreed safety plan.','教练因队员们无视商定的安全方案而严肃地批评了他们。','reprove someone for + fault','动词：以严肃、不赞同的态度指出某人的过失。','coach criticizes unsafe conduct.','书面'),M('The coach reproved the players by congratulating them for breaking the safety rules.','The coach reproved the players for breaking the safety rules.','表扬违规行为不是批评过失。','meaning'),[Q(1,'To reprove players for unsafe conduct is to…','criticize them seriously for the fault','reward them for the conduct','reproduce their conduct on video only','Reprove means criticize with disapproval.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which construction is correct?','reprove a student for cheating','reprove a student of cheat to','reprove for cheating a student at','The cause of criticism is introduced with for.','grammar'),Q(1,'A manager tells an employee that falsifying a report was wrong. The manager…','reproves the employee','reprints the report','reprocesses the employee','The manager expresses serious disapproval of a fault.','context'),Q(1,'Reprove is closest in meaning to…','rebuke','approve','reproduce','To reprove is to rebuke or criticize.','meaning')]);
P('reptile','From Latin reptilis “creeping,” from repere “crawl”; a reptile is a cold-blooded vertebrate such as a snake or crocodile, typically with scaly skin.',C('reptile.s1','自然','A lizard is a reptile, so the keeper provides a warm lamp and a dry hiding place.','蜥蜴是爬行动物，因此饲养员为它准备了保温灯和干燥的藏身处。','a reptile such as + animal','名词：如蛇、蜥蜴或鳄鱼等有鳞皮肤的变温脊椎动物。','lizard has reptile traits.','自然'),M('The keeper classified the furry, warm-blooded rabbit as a reptile because it had scales.','The keeper classified the scaly, cold-blooded lizard as a reptile.','兔子是哺乳动物；句中也没有鳞片。','distinction'),[Q(1,'Which animal is a reptile?','a crocodile','a sparrow','a dolphin','Crocodiles are reptiles; birds and mammals are not.','meaning'),Q(1,'A reptile commonly has…','scaly skin and a body temperature influenced by its surroundings','feathers and a constant internal temperature','fur and mammary glands','These are typical features of reptiles.','context'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','a reptile such as a lizard','a reptile such as a robin','a reptile with warm feathers','A lizard is an example of a reptile.','collocation'),Q(1,'The word reptile is linked to a Latin word meaning…','creeping','singing','governing','The Latin source refers to crawling or creeping.','word-formation')]);
P('reptilian','From reptile + -ian, based on Latin reptilis “creeping”; reptilian means relating to or resembling reptiles, and can describe behavior as cold or unpleasant.',C('reptilian.s1','生物','The fossil shows a reptilian jaw with rows of sharp, backward-curving teeth.','这块化石显示出爬行动物的颌骨，上面排列着向后弯曲的尖牙。','reptilian skin/jaw/behavior','形容词：属于或类似蛇、蜥蜴、鳄鱼等爬行动物的。','jaw has reptile anatomy.','生物'),M('The zoologist called the mammal’s furry coat reptilian, even though it had no features of a reptile.','The zoologist called the scaly jaw reptilian because it resembled that of a reptile.','毛皮而非爬行动物特征不支持此描述。','meaning'),[Q(1,'A reptilian jaw is one that…','belongs to or resembles a reptile','belongs to a flowering plant','represents an elected government','Reptilian means of or like a reptile.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','reptilian scales','reptilely scales','reptilian of scales at','Reptilian is an adjective modifying scales.','grammar'),Q(1,'A character described as having a reptilian manner may be portrayed as…','cold or unpleasant','warm and openly affectionate','a representative of parliament','The word can be used figuratively for cold behavior.','context'),Q(1,'Reptilian is formed from…','reptile + -ian','repression + -al','represent + -ive','The suffix -ian forms an adjective from reptile.','word-formation')]);
P('republic','From Latin res publica “public affair,” from res “thing” + publica “public”; a republic is a state governed by the people and elected leaders, or that form of government.',[C('republic.s1','政治','The constitution declares the country a republic with an elected president.','宪法规定该国为共和国，由民选总统执政。','a republic with + elected office','名词：权力由人民及其选举出的领导人掌握的国家。','president is elected.','政治'),C('republic.s2','政治','The debate concerned whether a republic should have a directly elected head of state.','这场辩论讨论共和国是否应设由全民直选的国家元首。','a republic as a system of government','名词：没有君主的共和政体。','discussion is about political system.','政治')],M('The constitution calls the country a republic even though its head of state inherits the throne as a monarch.','The constitution calls the country a republic because its head of state is elected rather than a hereditary monarch.','世袭君主与共和国的政体定义相矛盾。','distinction'),[Q(1,'A republic is generally governed by…','the people and elected leaders','a hereditary king or queen alone','a reptile as head of state','Sense 1 is a state whose authority comes from the people and elected leaders.','meaning'),Q(2,'Republic as a form of government means…','a system without a monarch','a system where every leader inherits a crown','a reprint of the constitution','Sense 2 names the political system itself.','context'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','a republic with an elected president','a republic of a hereditary king alone','republican a republicly state','A republic may have an elected president.','grammar'),Q(1,'The Latin phrase res publica is commonly glossed as…','public affair','private animal','new printing','It is the historical source of republic.','word-formation')]);
P('republican','From republic + -an, ultimately from Latin res publica “public affair”; republican can mean a supporter of the U.S. Republican Party, a supporter of elected government rather than monarchy, or related to a republic.',[C('republican.s1','通用','The Republican spoke at a local party meeting before the election.','这名共和党人在选举前出席了当地党部会议并发表讲话。','a Republican candidate/voter','名词：美国共和党成员或支持者。','party supporter speaks.','政治'),C('republican.s2','通用','The republican argued that the head of state should be chosen by voters rather than inherited.','这位共和主义者主张国家元首应由选民选出，而非世袭。','a republican system/argument','名词：支持由选举领导人执政、反对君主世袭的人。','advocates elected rule.','政治'),C('republican.s3','通用','The constitution established republican institutions and an elected legislature.','宪法建立了共和制度和民选立法机构。','republican values/institutions','形容词：与共和国或共和价值观有关。','institutions are part of republic.','政治')],M('The republican constitution transferred all authority to an unelected hereditary monarch and abolished elected offices.','The republican constitution based public authority on elected offices rather than a hereditary monarch.','世袭君主独揽权力与共和制度相悖。','meaning'),[Q(1,'In a U.S. election, a Republican is…','a member or supporter of the Republican Party','any elected head of state in a republic','a person who reprints a ballot','Sense 1 refers to the U.S. political party.','meaning'),Q(2,'A republican who opposes hereditary monarchy supports…','rule by elected leaders','a throne passed only by inheritance','the reprocessing of election materials','Sense 2 is a supporter of elected government rather than a monarch.','context'),Q(3,'Republican institutions are…','institutions related to a republic','institutions that must have a king','documents printed again','Sense 3 is the adjective meaning relating to a republic.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','a republican constitution','a republicly constitution','a republican of constitution','Republican is an adjective modifying constitution.','grammar')]);
P('republish','From re- “again” + publish, from Latin publicare “make public”; republish means issue a text or other work once more in print or online.',C('republish.s1','出版','The magazine will republish the interview online for readers who missed the first release.','杂志将在线重新刊登这篇访谈，让错过首次发布的读者也能阅读。','republish an article/book online','动词：再次出版或发表已发布过的作品。','article is issued a second time.','出版'),M('The magazine republished the interview by publishing it for the first time and never having released it before.','The magazine republished the interview after its original issue had appeared last year.','首次发表是 publish；republish 必须是再次发表。','distinction'),[Q(1,'A magazine republishes an interview when it…','issues the interview again','writes an unrelated interview from scratch','reprimands the interviewer','Republish means publish a work another time.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','republish the article online','republish online the first time only','republish the article into a reprint','The work has already been published and is issued again.','collocation'),Q(1,'A newspaper makes a past story available to a new audience. It…','republishes the story','represses the story','repots the story','Republishing gives an existing work another public release.','context'),Q(1,'What does re- mean in republish?','again','against','without','It indicates publication once more.','word-formation')]);
P('repudiate','From Latin repudiare “reject, divorce,” from repudi- “divorce”; repudiate means deny a claim, refuse to honor an obligation, or break away from a person or belief.',[C('repudiate.s1','通用','The scientist repudiated the claim after the original data were shown to be fabricated.','原始数据被证明是伪造的后，科学家否认了这一说法。','repudiate a claim/idea','动词：拒绝承认某项说法或观点为真。','claim is rejected as false.','通用'),C('repudiate.s2','商务','The company repudiated the contract and refused to pay the agreed fee.','公司拒绝履行合同，并拒绝支付约定费用。','repudiate a contract/debt/obligation','动词：拒绝履行协议、义务或偿还债务。','agreement is not honored.','商务'),C('repudiate.s3','通用','After the scandal, the candidate repudiated the group that had once supported him.','丑闻发生后，这名候选人与曾经支持他的团体断绝了关系。','repudiate a person/group/belief','动词：彻底与某人、群体或信仰决裂。','candidate breaks with group.','通用')],M('The company repudiated the contract by paying every agreed amount on time and confirming that it would honor all terms.','The company repudiated the contract by refusing to carry out its payment obligations.','按期履行所有条款是遵守合同，不是拒绝履行。','meaning'),[Q(1,'A scientist repudiates a claim when the scientist…','refuses to accept it as true','confirms it with new evidence','reprints it without comment','Sense 1 means reject a claim or idea.','meaning'),Q(2,'A company repudiates a debt when it…','refuses to pay or honor the obligation','pays it in full as agreed','asks for a copy of the contract','Sense 2 concerns rejecting an obligation.','context'),Q(3,'A candidate repudiates a former group by…','breaking away from it completely','joining it again after a brief absence','issuing its newsletter again','Sense 3 means disown or break with someone or a belief.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which construction is correct?','repudiate the allegation','repudiate to the allegation','repudiation the allegationly','Repudiate takes the claim or obligation as a direct object.','grammar')]);
P('repulse','From Latin repellere “drive back,” through French repousser; repulse means drive away an attack, coldly refuse an offer, or a rejection or act of driving back.',[C('repulse.s1','通用','The defenders repulsed the attack before it reached the city wall.','守军在进攻抵达城墙前将其击退。','repulse an attack/assault','动词：击退进攻或敌人。','defense drives attackers back.','军事'),C('repulse.s2','通用','She repulsed the offer with a brief note saying she was not interested.','她用一张简短便条冷淡地回绝了这份提议，表示自己不感兴趣。','repulse an offer/advance','动词：冷淡地拒绝提议或示好。','offer receives cold refusal.','通用'),C('repulse.s3','通用','The first repulse did not stop the rescuers from trying to reach the stranded climbers.','第一次受挫并未阻止救援人员继续尝试接近被困的登山者。','a repulse of + attack/advance','名词：击退进攻或拒绝提议的行为。','first attempt is driven back.','通用')],M('The defenders repulsed the attack by welcoming the attackers inside and letting them take the city.','The defenders repulsed the attack by forcing the attackers to retreat.','欢迎攻击者进城不是击退攻击。','meaning'),[Q(1,'The defenders repulsed an attack when they…','drove the attackers back','invited the attackers to occupy the city','requested a reservation','Repulse sense 1 means drive back an attack.','meaning'),Q(2,'She repulsed an offer with a cold note. She…','refused the offer sharply','accepted it enthusiastically','republished it online','Sense 2 is a cold rejection.','context'),Q(3,'A repulse in a battle is…','an act of driving an attack back','a guaranteed victory without fighting','a medical reproduction','The noun can name an act of repelling an enemy.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','repulse an assault','repulse at an assault it','repulse the assault to into','Repulse takes the attack as a direct object.','grammar')]);
P('repulsion','From repulse + -ion, from Latin repellere “drive back”; repulsion is a force that pushes like charges apart or a strong feeling of disgust.',[C('repulsion.s1','科学','The repulsion between the two like-charged particles pushed them apart.','两个同号带电粒子之间的排斥力使它们彼此分开。','repulsion between + objects/charges','名词：物理上使同类电荷或磁极相互推开的力。','like charges repel.','物理'),C('repulsion.s1','通用','She felt repulsion at the sight of the spoiled food and moved the plate away.','看到变质的食物，她感到厌恶，便把盘子移开。','feel repulsion at/toward + thing','名词：强烈的厌恶感。','food triggers disgust.','通用')],M('The repulsion between like charges pulled the particles together into a single point.','The repulsion between like charges pushed the particles apart.','同号电荷相互排斥，不会因此彼此吸引。','meaning'),[Q(1,'In physics, repulsion between like charges makes them…','push apart','attract one another','reproduce','Repulsion is a force that drives similar charges apart.','meaning'),Q(1,'She felt repulsion at the spoiled food. She felt…','strong disgust','a sense of relief','admiration for its freshness','The everyday sense of repulsion is intense dislike or disgust.','context'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','repulsion between the magnets','repulsion to the magnets between by','repulsive between magnetsly','Repulsion commonly takes between to name the objects involved.','grammar'),Q(1,'Which is an opposite feeling to repulsion?','attraction','disgust','rejection','Repulsion is a pushing-away force or feeling, unlike attraction.','meaning')]);
P('repulsive','From repulse + -ive, from Latin repellere “drive back”; repulsive means causing strong disgust or pushing things apart rather than attracting them.',[C('repulsive.s1','通用','The repulsive odor from the spoiled fish forced the crew to open every window.','变质鱼发出的恶臭让船员们不得不打开所有窗户。','repulsive smell/behavior','形容词：令人强烈厌恶的。','odor causes disgust.','通用'),C('repulsive.s2','科学','Like poles of the magnets exert a repulsive force on each other.','磁铁的同名磁极彼此施加排斥力。','repulsive force/interaction','形容词：使物体相互推开的，而非相互吸引的。','like poles push apart.','科学')],M('The repulsive odor was pleasant and made everyone eager to breathe it in.','The repulsive odor was so unpleasant that everyone moved away from it.','令人愉悦的气味与 repulsive 的厌恶义相反。','meaning'),[Q(1,'A repulsive smell is…','extremely unpleasant','fresh and attractive to everyone','a reserved seat','Sense 1 describes something causing disgust.','meaning'),Q(2,'A repulsive force between two like poles…','pushes them apart','pulls them together','makes them reproduce','Sense 2 is the physical opposite of an attractive force.','context'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','repulsive behavior','repulsionly behavior','behavior repulsive to in','Repulsive is an adjective modifying behavior.','grammar'),Q(1,'Which word is closest to repulsive in the everyday sense?','disgusting','appealing','reputable','Repulsive describes something that causes strong dislike.','meaning')]);
P('reputable','From repute + -able, from Latin reputare “think over, reckon”; reputable means respected because a person’s conduct or work is honest and of good quality.',C('reputable.s1','通用','We chose a reputable repair shop with clear prices and a long record of reliable service.','我们选择了一家信誉良好的维修店，它价格透明，服务可靠且经营多年。','a reputable company/source/dealer','形容词：因诚实可靠或质量高而受到尊重的。','shop has trustworthy record.','通用'),M('The guide recommended a reputable dealer despite knowing it routinely sold stolen goods and falsified its records.','The guide recommended a reputable dealer known for honest service and accurate records.','售赃并伪造记录的商家不具备良好声誉。','meaning'),[Q(1,'A reputable repair shop is one that…','is respected for reliable and honest work','is known for cheating its customers','repulses every customer','Reputable describes a business with a good reputation.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','a reputable source of information','a reputation source reputablely','a reputable of information source','Reputable is an adjective before source.','grammar'),Q(1,'A buyer checks reviews and licensing before choosing a trustworthy dealer. The buyer wants a…','reputable dealer','reputed rumor','repulsive dealer','A reputable dealer is respected for reliable conduct.','context'),Q(1,'Reputable is formed from repute plus…','-able','-less','-ing','The suffix -able creates the adjective reputable.','word-formation')]);
P('reputation','From Latin reputatio “consideration, reckoning,” from reputare; reputation is the general opinion people hold about someone or something, including its degree of trust or admiration.',[C('reputation.s1','通用','The restaurant built a reputation for generous portions and careful service.','这家餐馆因分量足、服务周到而建立了声誉。','a reputation for + quality; reputation of + person','名词：公众对个人、地点或公司的总体看法。','customers know restaurant’s traits.','通用'),C('reputation.s2','社会','The scientist’s reputation for honesty made other researchers trust her results.','这位科学家以诚实著称，因此其他研究人员信任她的结果。','a good/bad reputation; reputation for trustworthiness','名词：某人或某物受信任、受赞赏的程度。','trust follows established record.','社会')],M('The restaurant’s reputation for careful service came entirely from repeated complaints about careless staff.','The restaurant’s reputation for careful service came from customers’ positive experiences.','反复投诉员工粗心无法支撑“服务周到”的声誉。','meaning'),[Q(1,'A restaurant’s reputation for generous portions is…','the general opinion people have about it','a reservation for every customer','a legal reprieve','Reputation is the view people generally hold of someone or something.','meaning'),Q(2,'A scientist with a reputation for honesty is…','widely trusted for being honest','known for falsifying all results','a representative of a restaurant','This sense concerns the degree to which someone is trusted.','context'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','a reputation for honesty','a reputation honesty by at','reputably of honesty','Reputation is commonly followed by for before a quality.','grammar'),Q(1,'A strong reputation is built on…','what people generally believe about past conduct','one unverified rumor only','a plant’s new pot','Reputation reflects public opinion shaped by behavior or performance.','meaning')]);
P('repute','From Latin reputare “think over, reckon”; repute means the general opinion people hold, or be widely believed to have a quality, sometimes without proof.',[C('repute.s1','书面','The old academy was a place of considerable repute among local musicians.','这所老学院在当地音乐家中颇有声望。','a person/place of good/high repute','名词：公众对某人或机构形成的名声或评价。','community regards academy highly.','书面'),C('repute.s2','书面','The manuscript is reputed to be the poet’s earliest surviving work.','据说这份手稿是这位诗人现存最早的作品。','be reputed to be/have + quality','动词：被普遍认为具有某种特点，未必已证实。','claim is reported but unconfirmed.','书面')],M('The manuscript is reputed to be the poet’s earliest work, and the sentence presents this as conclusively proven fact.','The manuscript is reputed to be the poet’s earliest work, though the claim has not been confirmed.','be reputed to 表示广泛传言或普遍认为，并不自动证明事实。','meaning'),[Q(1,'A college of good repute is…','widely thought well of','known by nobody and never evaluated','a reprint of a diploma','Repute as a noun means standing or reputation.','meaning'),Q(2,'A manuscript is reputed to be ancient. This means…','many people say it is ancient, though it may be unproved','it is certainly proven ancient','it has been repotted','Reputed to be reports a commonly held but uncertain belief.','context'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','a person of high repute','a person on high reputedly','a repute personing','Repute as a noun commonly appears in “of good/high repute.”','grammar'),Q(1,'Which phrase signals an unconfirmed public belief?','is reputed to be','has been required to','is repressive of','Reputed to be marks what is widely believed, not necessarily proved.','meaning')]);
P('reputed','From repute + -ed; repute is from Latin reputare “think over.” Reputed means generally said or believed to have a stated quality or identity, without the speaker asserting proof.',C('reputed.s1','通用','The reputed author of the anonymous letter has not confirmed writing it.','这封匿名信据称的作者尚未承认是自己所写。','the reputed owner/author; reputed to be','形容词：据说具有某种身份或特点，但说话者未必证明属实。','identity is reported, not confirmed.','通用'),M('The reputed owner was identified in a rumor, so the identity was stated as fully verified beyond doubt.','The reputed owner was named in reports, but the identity had not been verified.','reputed 表示传闻中的身份，不能仅凭传闻说已确证。','meaning'),[Q(1,'The reputed author of a letter is…','the person said to have written it','the person proven to have written it in every case','the person who reprints it','Reputed indicates a commonly reported but not necessarily proven identity.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','the reputed owner of the house','the repute owner of house','the reputedly of the house owner','Reputed is an adjective modifying owner.','grammar'),Q(1,'A newspaper says someone is the reputed source of a leak, but the person denies it. “Reputed” means…','reported or believed to be the source','definitely proven to be the source','officially reprimanded for it','The claim is presented as a report, not established fact.','context'),Q(1,'Reputed is formed from…','repute + -ed','request + -ion','repress + -ive','The adjective uses the past-participle suffix -ed.','word-formation')]);
P('request','From Old French requeste, from Latin requirere “seek, ask for”; request means ask politely or officially, or the thing that is asked for.',[C('request.s1','正式','The committee requested that the supplier submit a revised safety report.','委员会正式要求供应商提交一份修订后的安全报告。','request that + clause; request something from someone','动词：以礼貌或正式方式提出要求。','committee makes formal ask.','正式'),C('request.s2','通用','At the audience’s request, the orchestra played the final movement again.','应观众的要求，管弦乐团再次演奏了最后一个乐章。','at someone’s request; a request for + item','名词：所请求的事物或事项。','audience asks for music.','通用')],M('The committee requested the supplier to submit a report, but then stated that it had made no request at all.','The committee requested a revised report from the supplier.','提出 request 与声称完全没有提出 request 自相矛盾。','meaning'),[Q(1,'The committee requested a revised report. It…','asked formally for the report','refused to accept any report','reprinted the old report without asking','Request as a verb is to ask politely or officially.','meaning'),Q(2,'A request from the audience is…','something the audience asked for','a statement the audience never made','a repressive law','Request as a noun can name the thing asked for.','context'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','at the audience’s request','on the audience requested','at request the audience’s of','The fixed pattern is at someone’s request.','collocation'),Q(1,'The supplier received a request for a report. What was received?','an ask for the report','the completed report necessarily','a new representative','A request is an act or item asked for, not necessarily the response.','meaning')]);
P('require','From Old French requerre, from Latin requirere “seek, ask for”; require means need something or make someone do something under a rule or order.',[C('require.s1','通用','This hiking route requires sturdy shoes and enough water for the full day.','这条徒步路线需要结实的鞋子和足够一天使用的饮用水。','require something for + purpose','动词：为了成功或存在而需要某物。','equipment is necessary.','通用'),C('require.s2','正式','The new policy requires all visitors to wear a badge inside the laboratory.','新规定要求所有访客在实验室内佩戴证件。','require someone to do something; be required by rule','动词：根据规则或命令要求某人做某事。','policy imposes rule.','正式')],M('The policy requires visitors to wear badges, yet it explicitly forbids them from wearing any badge.','The policy requires visitors to wear badges while they are inside the laboratory.','同一规定同时要求佩戴又禁止佩戴，互相矛盾。','meaning'),[Q(1,'A difficult hike requires sturdy shoes. The shoes are…','necessary for the hike','optional and unrelated','a request for a reservation','Sense 1 means need something.','meaning'),Q(2,'A policy requires visitors to wear badges. Visitors…','must wear them under the rule','may ignore the rule without consequence','are asked to reprint the policy','Sense 2 is a rule demanding an action.','context'),Q(1,'Which construction is correct?','require visitors to sign in','require visitors signing in to','require to visitors sign in','Require is followed by an object and an infinitive.','grammar'),Q(1,'Which sentence uses require as “need”?','The repair requires a new battery.','The guard requires everyone to sign in.','The memo requests a new date.','The first sentence describes something necessary for the repair.','meaning')]);
P('required','From require + -ed; require comes from Latin requirere “seek, ask for.” Required means needed by a rule or by a particular situation.',C('required.s1','教育','A signed permission form is required before the students can join the field trip.','学生参加实地考察前必须提交签字的许可表。','required by + rule; be required to do','形容词：规则或情形要求必须具备或完成的。','form is compulsory.','教育'),M('The permission form was required, but the school let every student join without submitting one.','The permission form was required, so students submitted it before joining.','如果完全不必提交，就不是 required。','meaning'),[Q(1,'A required form is one that…','must be submitted','is entirely optional','is a reprint only','Required means needed or compulsory.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','the required reading for the course','the require reading by the course','requiredly read course at','Required is an adjective modifying reading.','grammar'),Q(1,'Students cannot join until they submit permission. The form is…','required','reputable','reptilian','The school makes it a necessary condition.','context'),Q(1,'Required is formed from…','require + -ed','request + -al','requisite + -ing','The adjective is the -ed form of require.','word-formation')]);
P('requirement','From require + -ment; require comes from Latin requirere “seek, ask for.” A requirement is something needed or something that must be fulfilled.',C('requirement.s1','教育','A basic requirement for the scholarship is completion of two science courses.','申请这项奖学金的一项基本条件是修完两门科学课程。','a requirement for + role/purpose; meet a requirement','名词：必须具备或完成的条件、事项。','courses are eligibility condition.','教育'),M('Completion of two science courses was listed as a requirement, but applicants were accepted even if they had taken none.','Completion of two science courses was a requirement that applicants had to meet.','允许完全未修课者通过，说明该条件并非实际要求。','meaning'),[Q(1,'A scholarship requirement is…','a condition applicants must meet','a benefit given to every applicant','a repulsive smell','Requirement names something needed or compulsory.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','meet the entry requirements','meet to the requirements entry of','requirementing the entry','One can meet or satisfy a requirement.','collocation'),Q(1,'Applicants must complete two courses to qualify. The courses are a…','requirement','reprint','reptile','They are a necessary condition for qualification.','context'),Q(1,'Requirement is formed from which verb?','require','republish','reproduce','The noun adds -ment to require.','word-formation')]);
P('requisite','From Latin requisitus, past participle of requirere “seek, ask for”; requisite means necessary as a condition of success or correctness, not merely useful.',C('requisite.s1','书面','A valid permit is requisite for operating the equipment in this restricted zone.','在这个限制区域内操作设备必须持有有效许可证。','requisite for + purpose; the requisite skills','形容词：为达到目的或确保正确所必需的。','permit is essential.','正式'),M('The permit was requisite for entry, but visitors could enter without one and faced no restriction.','The permit was requisite for entry, so visitors had to show it at the gate.','若入场无需许可证，它就不是必要条件。','meaning'),[Q(1,'A requisite permit is…','necessary for the activity','merely decorative','a polite request for a permit','Requisite means required as a necessary condition.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','the requisite safety training','the requisite to safety trainings','requisitely safety training','Requisite can directly modify a noun such as training.','grammar'),Q(1,'A candidate cannot take the exam without an ID. The ID is…','requisite','reputed','residual','It is necessary for taking the exam.','context'),Q(1,'Which word is closest to requisite?','necessary','optional','repulsive','Requisite means required or necessary.','meaning')]);
P('requisition','From Latin requisitio “asking for,” from requirere; requisition is an official written request, official taking of property for public use, or formally demand supplies.',[C('requisition.s1','通用','The department submitted a requisition for replacement lab gloves.','该部门提交了更换实验室手套的正式申请单。','submit/file a requisition for + supplies','名词：对所需物品提出的正式书面申请。','department requests supplies formally.','通用'),C('requisition.s2','通用','During the emergency, authorities requisitioned several trucks for evacuation work.','紧急情况下，当局征用了几辆卡车用于疏散工作。','requisition property/vehicles for + purpose','名词：官方为军事或公共用途征用财物。','government takes vehicles.','社会'),C('requisition.s3','通用','The hospital requisitioned extra oxygen tanks from the regional depot.','医院向地区仓库正式调拨了额外氧气罐。','requisition supplies from + source','动词：正式要求或调拨物资。','hospital demands supplies officially.','医疗')],M('The authorities requisitioned the trucks by asking their owners to keep them privately and never use them for public work.','The authorities requisitioned the trucks for public evacuation work.','征用意味着官方调来财物供公共用途，而非要求私藏不用。','meaning'),[Q(1,'A supply requisition is…','an official written request for needed items','a receipt showing that items were rejected','an informal family greeting','Sense 1 is a formal request form.','meaning'),Q(2,'Authorities requisition trucks during an emergency when they…','officially take them for public use','sell them back to the original owners','reschedule the evacuation','Sense 2 is official taking of property.','context'),Q(3,'A hospital requisitions oxygen tanks from a depot. It…','formally demands or allocates the supplies','republishes the hospital rules','reproaches the depot','Sense 3 is to request supplies officially.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','submit a requisition for equipment','submit a requisition the equipment at','requisition for submit equipment a','A requisition is submitted for items needed.','grammar')]);
P('requital','From requite + -al; requite is from Old English gecwīdan “repay, answer.” Requital is something returned for a benefit or a wrong, either repayment or retaliation.',C('requital.s1','书面','The villagers viewed the generous harvest as requital for years of patient care of the land.','村民们认为，这次丰收是多年悉心照料土地所得到的回报。','requital for + service/wrong','名词：对恩惠或伤害所作的回报，可能是报答也可能是报复。','benefit receives return.','书面'),M('His requital for their help was to refuse every form of thanks and give nothing in return.','His requital for their help was to support them when they needed assistance.','完全不给予任何回报，不符合 requital 的含义。','meaning'),[Q(1,'Requital for a helpful act is…','something given in return','a requirement for a passport','a reptile species','Requital names a return made for a benefit or wrong.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','requital for their years of service','requital to service years by','requitaling their service out','For introduces the deed or benefit answered by requital.','grammar'),Q(1,'A community repays a benefactor’s help with support. The support is…','requital','repression','reproduction','It is a return for a previous benefit.','context'),Q(1,'Requital can mean repayment or…','retaliation','rescheduling','representation','A return for a wrong may take the form of revenge.','meaning')]);
P('reradiate','From re- “again” + radiate, from Latin radius “ray”; reradiate means emit again energy that has previously been absorbed, often as heat or radiation.',C('reradiate.s1','科学','After absorbing sunlight during the day, the pavement reradiates heat into the air at night.','白天吸收阳光后，路面会在夜间把热量再次辐射到空气中。','reradiate absorbed energy/heat','动词：把先前吸收的热或辐射重新释放出来。','surface emits stored heat.','科学'),M('The pavement reradiated heat even though it had absorbed no energy and emitted nothing.','The pavement absorbed sunlight and later reradiated some of that energy as heat.','没有吸收也没有发出能量，不符合“再辐射”。','meaning'),[Q(1,'A surface reradiates energy when it…','emits again energy it previously absorbed','absorbs energy and keeps all of it forever','prints a radiation report again','Reradiate specifically involves emitting absorbed energy again.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','reradiate absorbed heat','reradiate at heat with no absorption','reradiate the heat into a pot soil','The energy being emitted was first absorbed.','grammar'),Q(1,'Pavement warms in sunlight and gives off heat after sunset. It…','reradiates energy','reproves the sun','reprocesses the pavement','The stored solar energy is emitted again as heat.','context'),Q(1,'What does re- contribute to reradiate?','again','not','between','The verb means radiate once more.','word-formation')]);
P('rerun','From re- “again” + run; rerun means run or operate something again, or a broadcast shown another time.',C('rerun.s1','媒体','The station will rerun the interview after the live broadcast was interrupted.','直播中断后，电视台将重播这段访谈。','rerun a program/show; a rerun of + program','动词/名词：再次播出节目，也指重播的节目。','recording airs again.','媒体'),M('The station reran the interview by broadcasting it for the first and only time.','The station reran the interview after its original broadcast.','首次播出不是重播。','distinction'),[Q(1,'A rerun of a television episode is…','a repeat broadcast of an earlier episode','a newly filmed episode never shown before','a formal requisition','Rerun as a noun means a program shown again.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','rerun the program tonight','rerun the program for the first time only','rerun at program the tonight to','The verb means show or operate the same thing again.','grammar'),Q(1,'A computer test gives inconsistent results, so the technician runs it again. The technician…','reruns the test','relegates the test','reproaches the test','Rerun can mean operate a test again.','context'),Q(1,'What does re- indicate in rerun?','again','under','without','The task is run another time.','word-formation')]);
P('resale','From re- “again” + sale; resale is the sale of something already bought, commonly by a later owner rather than its maker.',C('resale.s1','商业','The resale of used textbooks helps students recover part of their costs.','转售旧课本能帮助学生收回部分费用。','resale value/market; resale of + item','名词：已购买商品后来再次出售。','books sold on by new owner.','商业'),M('The resale market includes only goods being sold by their original manufacturers for the first time.','The resale market includes goods that buyers sell again after purchasing them.','制造商首次出售是初次销售，不是 resale。','distinction'),[Q(1,'The resale of a used phone is…','a later sale of an item already purchased','the phone’s first sale by its maker','a requirement to repair it','Resale is a further sale after an initial purchase.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','the resale value of the bicycle','the resell value of the bicyclely','resale to bicycle the value on','Resale value names what the item may fetch when sold again.','collocation'),Q(1,'A student sells last year’s textbooks to a new owner. This is…','resale','repression','reproduction','The books are being sold for a second time.','context'),Q(1,'Which prefix in resale means “again”?','re-','un-','mis-','Resale combines re- with sale.','word-formation')]);
P('reschedule','From re- “again” + schedule, from Latin schedula “small sheet”; reschedule means set a new time or date for an already planned event.',C('reschedule.s1','通用','The clinic rescheduled my appointment for Friday because the doctor was ill.','医生生病后，诊所把我的预约改到了星期五。','reschedule an appointment/meeting for + time','动词：把已有安排改到另一个时间。','appointment moves to new date.','通用'),M('The clinic rescheduled my appointment by keeping it at exactly the same time and making no change.','The clinic rescheduled my appointment by moving it to Friday.','没有变更时间就不是改期。','meaning'),[Q(1,'The clinic rescheduled the appointment. It…','set it for a different time','cancelled every future appointment permanently','reprinted the appointment card only','Reschedule means arrange a new time for something planned.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','reschedule the interview for Friday','reschedule Friday the interview to on','reschedule the interview for its old time unchanged','For can introduce the new date or time.','grammar'),Q(1,'A flight is moved from Monday to Tuesday. The airline…','reschedules the flight','resells the flight','reproaches the flight','A new time has been assigned to a planned event.','context'),Q(1,'What does re- mean in reschedule?','again or anew','below','without','The plan is scheduled again for a different time.','word-formation')]);
P('rescue','From Old French rescourre “free, release,” from Latin excutere “shake off”; rescue means save a person, animal, or thing from danger or a bad situation, or the act of doing so.',[C('rescue.s1','通用','Firefighters rescued two residents from the upper floor of the burning house.','消防员从着火房屋的楼上救出了两名居民。','rescue someone from + danger/place','动词：使人、动物或物品脱离危险或困境。','firefighters save people.','安全'),C('rescue.s2','通用','The rescue of the stranded hikers took six hours in heavy snow.','大雪中，救援被困徒步者的行动持续了六个小时。','a rescue operation; the rescue of + person','名词：把人从危险中救出的行动。','operation brings hikers to safety.','安全')],M('The firefighters rescued the residents by leaving them trapped in the burning house.','The firefighters rescued the residents by bringing them safely out of the burning house.','让居民继续被困在火场中不是救援。','meaning'),[Q(1,'Firefighters rescued the residents when they…','brought them out of danger','left them trapped upstairs','rescheduled their visit','Rescue as a verb means save from danger.','meaning'),Q(2,'A rescue operation is…','an act of saving people from danger','a request for new equipment only','a report that no one was in danger','Rescue as a noun names the saving action.','context'),Q(1,'Which construction is correct?','rescue a swimmer from the current','rescue from the current a swimmer to','rescue a swimmer at current into','From introduces the danger or place someone is saved from.','grammar'),Q(1,'A dog is pulled from a flooded ditch and taken to safety. This is a…','rescue','reprieve','resale','The action saves an animal from a dangerous situation.','context')]);
P('research','From Middle French recerche “search,” from rechercher “search closely”; research is careful study to discover facts or understanding, or the act of studying a subject in that way.',[C('research.s1','学术','The team’s research compared air samples from the city center and nearby farms.','研究团队比较了市中心和附近农场采集的空气样本。','conduct/carry out research on/into + topic','名词：为发现事实或新认识而进行的仔细研究。','study compares collected samples.','学术'),C('research.s2','学术','Before choosing a treatment, the doctor researched the latest clinical guidance.','选择治疗方案前，医生研究了最新的临床指南。','research a topic/source','动词：仔细研究某主题以发现事实。','doctor studies information.','医学')],M('The team’s research compared no samples and collected no information, yet it claimed to discover new evidence.','The team’s research compared carefully collected samples to find evidence.','没有研究材料或信息搜集，不能支撑发现新证据。','meaning'),[Q(1,'Scientific research is…','careful study to discover facts','an appointment kept for a visitor','a reprint of a novel','Research sense 1 names systematic investigation.','meaning'),Q(2,'The doctor researched treatment guidance by…','studying it carefully','reselling it to patients','repressing the guidance','Research as a verb means study a subject closely.','context'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','research into air quality','research to air quality into','a research into carefullyly','One can conduct research into a subject.','collocation'),Q(1,'Which sentence uses research as a verb?','She researched the topic before the interview.','Her research lasted a year.','The research was published.','In the first sentence, researched describes an action.','grammar')]);
P('researcher','From research + -er; research is from French rechercher “search closely.” A researcher is someone who studies a subject carefully to discover facts or new understanding.',C('researcher.s1','教育','The researcher interviewed residents to learn how the new bus route affected them.','研究人员采访了居民，了解新公交线路对他们的影响。','a researcher in/on + field','名词：为发现事实或新认识而研究某个主题的人。','interviewing supports a study.','教育'),M('The researcher published findings without studying the subject, collecting information, or examining evidence.','The researcher studied the subject and examined evidence before publishing findings.','没有进行研究就不能据此称为研究人员。','meaning'),[Q(1,'A researcher is someone who…','studies a subject to discover facts','only resells used goods','is a resident who avoids all questions','The noun names a person who conducts research.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','a researcher in marine biology','a researchly in marine biology','a researcher of to marine biology','Researcher can be followed by in to name a field.','grammar'),Q(1,'A scientist collects data to understand a disease. The scientist is a…','researcher','reputable','reptile','The scientist studies a subject to discover new facts.','context'),Q(1,'The suffix -er in researcher refers to…','a person who researches','a place where research happens','a past-tense action','The suffix commonly forms an agent noun from research.','word-formation')]);
P('resell','From re- “again” + sell, from Old English sellan “give, sell”; resell means sell again an item one has already bought.',C('resell.s1','商业','The shop lets customers resell their used cameras after upgrading to a newer model.','顾客换用新型号后，可以把旧相机转卖给这家商店。','resell an item to someone; resell for + price','动词：把已经购买过的东西再次卖出。','used camera changes owner again.','商业'),M('He resold the camera by keeping it and never offering it to another buyer.','He resold the camera by selling it to another buyer after purchasing it.','保留物品且未出售，不是转售。','meaning'),[Q(1,'To resell a camera is to…','sell it again after buying it','buy it for the first time','repair it without changing ownership','Resell is a further sale of a purchased item.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','resell a used bicycle online','resell to bicycle the used','resell the bicycle at its first sale','The item is sold again to another buyer.','grammar'),Q(1,'A traveler buys a ticket and later sells it to someone else. The traveler…','resells the ticket','reprocesses the ticket','reproves the ticket','The already purchased ticket is being sold again.','context'),Q(1,'What does re- mean in resell?','again','between','not','The item is sold once more.','word-formation')]);
P('resemblance','From resemble + -ance, from Old French resembler; resemblance is the fact that things look or seem alike, or a particular feature they share.',[C('resemblance.s1','通用','There is a strong resemblance between the twins, especially around the eyes.','这对双胞胎长相很像，尤其是眼睛周围。','resemblance between A and B','名词：两个人或事物看起来相似的事实。','twins have similar appearance.','通用'),C('resemblance.s2','通用','The resemblance in the two paintings lies in their use of the same dark blue palette.','这两幅画相似之处在于它们都使用了同一组深蓝色调。','a resemblance in + feature; resemblance to + model','名词：两件事物具体相像的方面。','shared feature is palette.','艺术')],M('The twins have a strong resemblance, although one has a completely different face and no similar features.','The twins have a strong resemblance, with similar eyes and facial features.','完全不同的长相与“很像”相矛盾。','meaning'),[Q(1,'A resemblance between twins is…','a similarity in how they look','a difference in their family names','a request from their teacher','Sense 1 names the fact that they seem alike.','meaning'),Q(2,'The resemblance in two paintings lies in their palette. This means…','the palette is one particular feature they share','the paintings are identical in every way','both painters live in the same residence','Sense 2 is a specific similarity.','context'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','a resemblance between the two designs','a resemblance among the two designs between','resemblance the designs to of','Between identifies the two things that look alike.','grammar'),Q(1,'Which word is closest to resemblance?','likeness','opposition','requisition','Resemblance means similarity or likeness.','meaning')]);
P('resemble','From Old French resembler “be like,” from re- + sembler; resemble means have a similar appearance or be similar in character, sound, or effect.',[C('resemble.s1','通用','The new library resembles the old station, with the same tall arched windows.','新图书馆与旧车站很像，都有高高的拱形窗户。','resemble someone/something','动词：外表与另一人或物相似。','buildings share visible features.','通用'),C('resemble.s2','通用','Her latest proposal resembles the earlier plan in its overall effect.','她最新的提案在整体效果上与早先的计划相似。','resemble something in + quality','动词：在性质、声音或效果上相似。','plans have similar effect.','通用')],M('The new library resembles the station because it has no features, colors, or shapes in common with it.','The new library resembles the station because both have tall arched windows.','毫无共同特征不能作为相似的依据。','meaning'),[Q(1,'The library resembles the old station. It…','looks similar to the station','is required to replace the station','is a resident of the station','Sense 1 concerns appearance.','meaning'),Q(2,'A proposal resembles an earlier plan in effect when…','their results are similar','their buildings look alike','one plan has been resold','Sense 2 concerns shared character or effect.','context'),Q(1,'Which sentence is grammatical?','The child resembles her aunt.','The child resembles to her aunt.','The child is resemble her aunt.','Resemble takes a direct object without to.','grammar'),Q(1,'A new tune has a similar sound to an older song. The tune…','resembles the older song','resides in the older song','reproaches the older song','Resemble can describe similarity in sound.','context')]);
P('resent','From French ressentir “feel keenly,” from re- + sentir “feel”; resent means feel bitter or angry because something seems unfair, including another person’s success or treatment.',[C('resent.s1','情感','She resented being left out of the planning meeting after doing most of the work.','做了大部分工作后却被排除在筹备会议之外，她对此感到愤愤不平。','resent being/doing; resent + unfair action','动词：因认为受到不公对待而感到愤怒和怨恨。','exclusion seems unfair.','情感'),C('resent.s2','情感','He resented his colleague’s promotion because he believed she had received unfair advantages.','他怨恨同事的晋升，因为他认为她获得了不公平的优待。','resent someone’s success/treatment','动词：对他人的成功或较好待遇感到不满。','promotion prompts bitterness.','情感')],M('She resented the unfair exclusion, but she was delighted and felt no bitterness about it.','She resented the unfair exclusion and felt bitter about being left out.','resent 表示愤懑，与“欣然且毫无怨气”不相符。','meaning'),[Q(1,'She resented being excluded after doing most of the work. She…','felt bitter because she thought it was unfair','was pleased that she was excluded','received a reprieve','Resent describes angry bitterness over perceived unfairness.','meaning'),Q(2,'He resented his colleague’s promotion because he felt…','the success or treatment was unfair','the promotion was a required form','the colleague resembled a relative','Sense 2 focuses on another person’s success or advantage.','context'),Q(1,'Which construction is natural?','resent being left out','resent to be left out of','resent about being out by','Resent can take a gerund as its object.','grammar'),Q(1,'Which word is closest to resent?','begrudge','admire','reproduce','To resent is to feel bitter about something seen as unfair.','meaning')]);
P('resentful','From resent + -ful; resent comes from French ressentir “feel keenly.” Resentful means feeling anger or bitterness because of unfair treatment.',C('resentful.s1','情感','The resentful employee believed that the promotion had been given unfairly.','这名愤愤不平的员工认为，晋升机会被不公平地给了别人。','feel/be resentful about/at + treatment','形容词：因觉得受到不公平对待而感到愤怒。','employee sees injustice.','情感'),M('She was resentful about the fair decision and felt completely satisfied with the unfair treatment.','She was resentful about the unfair decision and felt she had been treated badly.','对公平结果毫无不满，与 resentful 的含义相反。','meaning'),[Q(1,'A resentful employee is likely to feel…','angry about perceived unfair treatment','grateful for unfair treatment','eager to reschedule a meeting','Resentful describes bitterness over an injury or injustice.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','resentful about the decision','resentful the decisionly','resentful to decision with','Resentful can be followed by about or at.','grammar'),Q(1,'A student thinks another student received an undeserved award and feels bitter. The student is…','resentful','reputable','resilient','The feeling is anger about perceived unfairness.','context'),Q(1,'Resentful is formed from resent plus…','-ful','-er','-ize','The suffix -ful forms an adjective describing the feeling.','word-formation')]);
P('resentment','From resent + -ment; resent comes from French ressentir “feel keenly.” Resentment is lasting anger or bitterness over a real or imagined injury.',C('resentment.s1','情感','Years of resentment built up after the manager repeatedly ignored her contributions.','经理多次忽视她的贡献后，多年来的怨恨逐渐累积起来。','resentment about/over + issue; resentment toward + person','名词：因真实或想象中的伤害而积存的愤怒与苦涩。','repeated slight builds anger.','情感'),M('The repeated unfair treatment caused no resentment because the employee felt bitter and angry about it.','The repeated unfair treatment caused resentment because the employee felt bitter and angry.','感到怨恨就表示存在 resentment，不能说毫无怨恨。','meaning'),[Q(1,'Resentment is…','anger and bitterness kept over an injury','a formal request for supplies','a successful rescue','It names a lasting bitter feeling.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','resentment over the unfair decision','resentment to over decisioning','resentful of the decision as a noun','Resentment can be followed by over to name its cause.','grammar'),Q(1,'A worker remains bitter for years after being repeatedly overlooked. This feeling is…','resentment','resemblance','residence','The bitterness has built up over a perceived wrong.','context'),Q(1,'Which verb is the base of resentment?','resent','reside','resell','Resentment is the noun formed from resent.','word-formation')]);
P('reservation','From reserve + -ation; reserve is from Latin reservare “keep back.” Reservation can mean a booked seat or room, a doubt, or land set aside by law for a group.',[C('reservation.s1','通用','I made a reservation for four at the restaurant for 7:30.','我预订了餐厅晚上七点半四人用餐的位置。','make a reservation for + time/party','名词：安排为某人保留座位或房间。','table is booked.','服务'),C('reservation.s2','通用','She accepted the plan, but had reservations about its cost and timing.','她接受了计划，但对成本和时间安排仍有疑虑。','have reservations about + plan','名词：认为某事未必完全妥当的理由或疑虑。','doubts remain.','通用'),C('reservation.s3','通用','The community’s reservation includes homes, schools, and protected land.','这个社区的保留地包括住宅、学校和受保护的土地。','a reservation for + community','名词：依法为特定群体保留的土地。','land is legally designated.','社会')],M('She made a reservation for dinner, but the restaurant had no record and had not held any table for her.','She made a reservation for dinner, and the restaurant held a table for her.','若没有安排保留座位，就没有完成预订。','meaning'),[Q(1,'A restaurant reservation means…','a table is arranged to be kept for someone','a concern about the menu','land set aside for a community','Sense 1 is a booking.','meaning'),Q(2,'If she has reservations about the plan, she…','has doubts about whether it is fully right','has already booked a seat','owns the plan completely','Sense 2 means doubts or concerns.','context'),Q(3,'A reservation for a community is…','land kept by law for that group','a hotel booking for every community member','an opinion about a dinner','Sense 3 refers to designated land.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','make a reservation for two','make a reservation about table of two to','reserve a reservation the two','One makes a reservation for the party or time.','grammar')]);
P('reserve','From Latin reservare “keep back,” from re- + servare “keep”; reserve means arrange a booking, keep something for later, or a stock/protected area/shy manner.',[C('reserve.s1','服务','Please reserve a quiet table near the window for our guests.','请为我们的客人预订一张靠窗的安静桌子。','reserve a seat/room/table for + person','动词：安排将座位、房间或桌子留给某人。','table is held for guests.','服务'),C('reserve.s2','正式','The hospital reserved extra masks for staff working in the emergency ward.','医院为急诊病房的工作人员预留了额外口罩。','reserve something for later/someone','动词：留出某物以供以后或特定的人使用。','masks kept for future use.','正式'),C('reserve.s3','通用','The region maintains a wildlife reserve and a reserve of emergency fuel.','该地区设有野生动物保护区，并储备了应急燃料。','a nature reserve; reserves of + resource','名词：留存的储备、保护区，也可指不轻易表露情感的矜持。','land protected; fuel kept.','通用')],M('The hospital reserved masks for the emergency ward by giving every mask away to unrelated visitors.','The hospital reserved masks for the emergency ward by setting them aside for its staff.','把物资送给无关人员不是为急诊预留。','meaning'),[Q(1,'To reserve a table for guests is to…','arrange for it to be kept for them','sell it to another restaurant','reprocess it after dinner','Reserve sense 1 means book or hold a place.','meaning'),Q(2,'The hospital reserved masks for later use. It…','kept them aside for a particular purpose','used them all immediately','reprimanded the staff','Sense 2 is keeping something for later.','context'),Q(3,'A wildlife reserve is…','a protected area for wildlife','a restaurant booking','a shy way of speaking','Sense 3 includes a protected area.','meaning'),Q(3,'A person who speaks with reserve tends to…','show feelings cautiously','talk freely to every stranger','store emergency fuel','Reserve as a noun can mean restrained behavior.','context')]);
P('reserved','From reserve + -ed; reserve is from Latin reservare “keep back.” Reserved means set aside for a particular person or quiet and unwilling to show feelings.',[C('reserved.s1','通用','The front row is reserved for families with young children.','前排座位为带幼儿的家庭预留。','reserved for + person/purpose','形容词：已经留给特定的人或用途，别人不可使用。','seats are set aside.','通用'),C('reserved.s2','性格','Although friendly, Arun is reserved and rarely talks about his private life.','阿伦虽然友善，却很内敛，很少谈论自己的私生活。','a reserved person/manner','形容词：不愿表露情感或自由交谈的。','person keeps feelings private.','性格')],M('The seats were reserved for the guests, but anyone could take them and no place was set aside.','The seats were reserved for the guests and kept unavailable to others.','若任何人都可随意使用，就没有为客人预留。','meaning'),[Q(1,'Reserved seats are seats…','set aside for particular people','available to everyone without limit','that have already been resold','Sense 1 means kept for someone.','meaning'),Q(2,'A reserved person is often…','slow to show feelings or talk freely','loud and immediately open with everyone','a hotel room','Sense 2 concerns a quiet or restrained manner.','context'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','a reserved seat for the speaker','a seat reservedly to the speaker','a seat of reserve for the speakerly','Reserved modifies seat and for identifies whom it is held for.','grammar'),Q(1,'Which word is closest to reserved in the personality sense?','reticent','talkative','required','Reserved people tend not to speak freely about themselves.','meaning')]);
P('reservoir','From French réservoir, from réserver “reserve,” ultimately from Latin reservare “keep back”; a reservoir is a lake or tank storing water, or a large supply of something available for use.',[C('reservoir.s1','地理','The new reservoir stores rainwater for farms and homes during the dry season.','这座新水库在旱季为农田和家庭储存雨水。','a reservoir of water; build a reservoir','名词：储存公共用水的湖泊，常为人工建成。','water is stored for later.','地理'),C('reservoir.s2','书面','The library has a reservoir of local stories that have never been published.','这家图书馆收藏着大量从未出版过的地方故事。','a reservoir of + knowledge/energy/resources','名词：可随时调用的大量资源或储备。','stories are abundant.','书面')],M('The reservoir supplied water during the drought even though it contained no stored water.','The reservoir supplied water during the drought from the water stored in it.','空水库无法提供其中并不存在的储水。','meaning'),[Q(1,'A water reservoir is…','a place where water is stored','a room booked for a guest','a formal reprimand','Sense 1 is a water-storage lake or tank.','meaning'),Q(2,'A reservoir of stories means…','a large supply of stories available to draw on','one unpublished story only','a lake full of paper','Sense 2 is a large store of something abstract.','context'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','a reservoir of fresh water','a reservoir with fresh waters are','reservoiring the water for fresh','Reservoir is commonly followed by of before its contents.','grammar'),Q(1,'An artificial lake stores water for later use. It is a…','reservoir','residence','reprint','Reservoir names a water-storage body.','meaning')]);
P('reset','From re- “again” + set, from Old English settan “put in place”; reset means set a device or value again to its original or a new position.',C('reset.s1','工具','Hold the button for five seconds to reset the router to its factory settings.','按住按钮五秒，将路由器重设为出厂设置。','reset a device/password/value','动词：再次设置某物，使其恢复原值或变成新值。','router returns to base settings.','工具'),M('She reset the router to factory settings by leaving every setting exactly as it was and changing nothing.','She reset the router by restoring its settings to the factory defaults.','完全不改变设置不是重设。','meaning'),[Q(1,'Resetting a router to factory settings…','sets it back to its original configuration','makes it impossible to use forever','reschedules the internet service','Reset means set again to an original or new value.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','reset your password','reset to your password again it','resetting password the yesterday','Reset takes the setting or device as an object.','grammar'),Q(1,'A timer is set to zero so it can begin a new count. The timer is…','reset','reserved','repulsed','It is returned to a starting value.','context'),Q(1,'Reset combines re- with…','set','sell','side','Reset means set again.','word-formation')]);
P('resettle','From re- “again” + settle, from Old English setlan “establish”; resettle means begin living in a new place after leaving a former home, or help people do so.',C('resettle.s1','社会','The aid agency helped families resettle in a nearby town after the flood destroyed their homes.','洪水摧毁家园后，救援机构帮助这些家庭在附近城镇重新定居。','resettle in + place; help someone resettle','动词：离开原住所后在别处开始生活。','families establish new homes.','社会'),M('The families resettled in a new town while continuing to live permanently in their destroyed former homes.','The families resettled in a new town after leaving their damaged homes.','在新地方重新安家意味着离开旧居，不是继续住在毁坏的原处。','meaning'),[Q(1,'Families resettle after a flood when they…','begin living in a new place','return to the same damaged home and never move','reprint their address','Resettle means settle again somewhere else.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','resettle in a nearby town','resettle at a town in to','resettle the town in a family','In introduces the new place of residence.','grammar'),Q(1,'An agency helps displaced people find homes in another country. It helps them…','resettle','reprove','reset the flood','The agency assists people to establish a new home.','context'),Q(1,'What does re- indicate in resettle?','again','without','against','The people settle again in a new place.','word-formation')]);
P('reshape','From re- “again” + shape, from Old English gesceap “form”; reshape means give something a new form or change its structure or direction in an important way.',C('reshape.s1','通用','The new director reshaped the department by combining two teams and changing their roles.','新主管通过合并两个团队并调整职责，重塑了部门。','reshape a plan/organization/structure','动词：改变形状、组织方式或发展方向。','department’s organization changes.','通用'),M('The director reshaped the department while keeping every role, structure, and direction exactly unchanged.','The director reshaped the department by changing its structure and roles.','各方面保持原样就没有发生重塑。','meaning'),[Q(1,'To reshape a department is to…','change its structure or organization','print the same chart again','give every worker a reservation','Reshape means change the form or structure.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','reshape public policy','reshape to public policying','shape again the policy reshape','Reshape takes the thing being changed as its direct object.','grammar'),Q(1,'A city changes zoning to encourage housing near transit. The policy may…','reshape urban development','resettle the transit','reproach housing','It changes the direction and structure of development.','context'),Q(1,'What does re- contribute to reshape?','anew or again','not','before','It indicates giving an existing thing a new shape.','word-formation')]);
P('reshuffle','From re- “again” + shuffle, an alteration of older shovelen “mix”; reshuffle means change people’s roles in a team or government, or mix cards and items again.',[C('reshuffle.s1','政治','The prime minister reshuffled the cabinet after two ministers resigned.','两名部长辞职后，首相改组了内阁。','reshuffle a cabinet/team; reshuffle posts','动词：重新安排政府或组织中人员担任的职务。','ministers change posts.','政治'),C('reshuffle.s2','政治','The reshuffle moved several senior officials to different departments.','这次改组把几名高级官员调到了不同部门。','a cabinet reshuffle; a reshuffle of + posts/cards','名词：职位调整，也可指再次混洗卡牌或物品。','posts are reorganized.','政治')],M('The prime minister reshuffled the cabinet by leaving every minister in exactly the same position and making no changes.','The prime minister reshuffled the cabinet by changing which ministers held several posts.','不作任何人员安排改变，就不是改组。','meaning'),[Q(1,'A prime minister reshuffles a cabinet when the prime minister…','changes who holds government posts','reprints a cabinet manual','resettles the entire country','Sense 1 is to reorganize official roles.','meaning'),Q(2,'A cabinet reshuffle is…','a change in who holds particular posts','a fixed arrangement that never changes','a reservation for a minister','The noun names a reorganization of roles.','context'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','reshuffle the cabinet','reshuffle to the cabinet into','reshufflingly the cabinets','Reshuffle takes the group or set of roles as its object.','grammar'),Q(2,'After a reshuffle, senior officials may…','hold different posts','remain in every identical role','become reptilian','A reshuffle changes the arrangement of positions.','meaning')]);
P('reside','From Latin residere “sit back, remain,” from re- + sedere “sit”; reside means live in a place, especially permanently, or exist within a person or thing.',[C('reside.s1','正式','The ambassador has resided in the capital for nearly three years.','这位大使已在首都居住了将近三年。','reside in + place','动词：在某地生活，尤指长期或永久居住。','ambassador lives in capital.','正式'),C('reside.s2','书面','The final authority to approve the budget resides in the elected council.','批准预算的最终权力属于民选委员会。','responsibility/authority resides in + person/group','动词：某种性质、权力或能力存在于某人或事物之中。','authority is located in council.','书面')],M('The ambassador resided in the capital for three years while living permanently in another country and never staying there.','The ambassador resided in the capital for three years and made it his home.','长期不在该地、不在当地居住，与 reside 不符。','meaning'),[Q(1,'The ambassador resides in the capital. The ambassador…','lives there','has a reservation there only','reprocesses the capital','Sense 1 means live in a place.','meaning'),Q(2,'Authority resides in the council means…','the council has or holds that authority','the council lives inside a house','the authority has been rescheduled','Sense 2 means a quality or power is present in something.','context'),Q(1,'Which construction is natural?','reside in the capital','reside at the capital in to','reside the capital','Reside is commonly followed by in before a place.','grammar'),Q(1,'The verb reside most directly means…','live','resell','reprove','The word refers to living in a place.','meaning')]);
P('residence','From Latin residentia, from residere “remain, dwell”; a residence is a place where someone lives, especially a large or grand house.',C('residence.s1','家居','The governor’s official residence stands beside the public gardens.','州长的官邸位于公共花园旁边。','a private/official residence; place of residence','名词：某人居住的地方，尤指较大的宅邸。','official home is large.','家居'),M('The family’s residence was the place where they never lived and which served only as an unoccupied warehouse.','The family’s residence was the house where they lived throughout the year.','完全无人居住、只作仓库之地不是这个家庭的住所。','meaning'),[Q(1,'An official residence is…','the home where an official lives','a request for an appointment','a person who studies research','Residence means a place where someone lives.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','her place of residence','her place reside of','residentially place residence','Residence is a noun naming a home or dwelling.','grammar'),Q(1,'A grand house where a royal family lives is a…','residence','residue','requisition','It is a place where people live.','context'),Q(1,'Residence is related to the verb…','reside','resent','reprint','A residence is where someone resides.','word-formation')]);
P('residency','From resident + -cy, from Latin residere “dwell”; residency can mean the right or fact of living in a place, a new doctor’s hospital training, or an artist’s live-work program.',[C('residency.s1','通用','The application asks applicants to prove their residency in the state.','申请表要求申请人证明自己在该州的居留身份。','residency in + place; establish residency','名词：在某地居住的事实或居留资格。','applicant proves local status.','通用'),C('residency.s2','通用','After medical school, he completed a residency in pediatrics at the city hospital.','医学院毕业后，他在市立医院完成了儿科住院医师培训。','a residency in + medical specialty','名词：新医生在医院接受的实践培训期。','doctor trains in hospital.','医学'),C('residency.s3','通用','The ceramic artist received a six-month residency at a rural arts center.','这位陶艺家获得了乡村艺术中心为期六个月的驻留项目。','an artist/writer residency; residency at + institution','名词：让艺术家等人在某地生活并工作的驻留项目。','artist lives and works there temporarily.','艺术')],M('The doctor completed a residency in pediatrics without receiving any practical hospital training.','The doctor completed a pediatrics residency through supervised hospital practice.','住院医师培训的核心是医院内实践训练。','meaning'),[Q(1,'Proof of residency in a state shows…','the right or fact of living there','completion of a medical exam','a reservation at a restaurant','Sense 1 concerns residence status.','meaning'),Q(2,'A doctor’s residency is…','a period of practical hospital training','a permanent appointment as governor','a research report reprinted','Sense 2 is postgraduate clinical training.','context'),Q(3,'An artist residency provides…','a place or program to live and work for a period','a legal order to leave art','a permanent house deed necessarily','Sense 3 is a temporary live-work arts program.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','complete a residency in surgery','residency to a surgery completing','complete residence surgery at residency','Medical residency is commonly completed in a specialty.','collocation')]);
P('resident','From Latin residens, present participle of residere “dwell”; a resident is someone who lives in a particular place for a long time.',C('resident.s1','社会','Every resident of the apartment building received a notice about the water shutdown.','公寓楼的每位居民都收到了停水通知。','a resident of + place','名词：在某地长期居住的人。','notice reaches people who live there.','社会'),M('The town’s residents were people who had never lived there and only visited once.','The town’s residents were people who lived there throughout the year.','只来访一次的人不是当地居民。','meaning'),[Q(1,'A resident of an apartment building is someone who…','lives there','repaired the building once','made a reservation there','Resident names someone who lives in a place.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','a resident of the town','a residence the town of','residently in the town of','The pattern resident of + place is common.','grammar'),Q(1,'A person lives in a village for many years. The person is a…','resident','requisition','reptile','Long-term residence makes the person a resident.','context'),Q(1,'Resident is related to the verb…','reside','reprint','resist','A resident is someone who resides in a place.','word-formation')]);
P('residential','From residence + -ial; residence comes from Latin residere “dwell.” Residential means designed for people to live in or providing a place to stay while studying or working.',[C('residential.s1','通用','The city changed the empty lot into a residential block with apartments and shops.','市政府把这块空地改建成了住宅区，里面有公寓和商店。','residential area/property/building','形容词：用于居住而非主要用于商业的。','apartments provide homes.','城市'),C('residential.s2','通用','The college runs a residential program where students live on campus during training.','这所学院开设寄宿项目，培训期间学生住在校园里。','a residential school/program/course','形容词：学习或工作期间提供住宿的。','students live where they study.','教育')],M('The residential program required students to live elsewhere and provided no place to stay.','The residential program provided students with rooms on campus during training.','完全不提供住宿的项目不属于 residential 的寄宿义。','meaning'),[Q(1,'A residential block is mainly designed for…','people to live in','industrial machinery only','a temporary research result','Sense 1 concerns housing.','meaning'),Q(2,'A residential training program provides…','a place to live while training','only online lessons with no accommodation','a rescheduled appointment','Sense 2 means accommodation is included.','context'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','a residential neighborhood','a residence neighborhoodly','a residential of neighborhood','Residential is an adjective modifying neighborhood.','grammar'),Q(1,'Which noun is residential related to?','residence','residue','resolve','Residential describes housing or living arrangements.','word-formation')]);
P('residents','From resident + plural -s; resident comes from Latin residere “dwell.” Residents are the people who live in a particular place or building.',C('residents.s1','社会','The residents of the coastal village met to plan a flood drill.','沿海村庄的居民聚在一起，商量防洪演练。','residents of + place/building','复数名词：居住在某地或某栋建筑里的所有人。','local people organize drill.','社会'),M('The building’s residents were tourists who had never lived there and left after one hour.','The building’s residents were people who lived there throughout the year.','短暂停留的游客不是住户。','meaning'),[Q(1,'Residents of a village are…','the people who live there','people who publish the village map','visitors who never stay','Residents are inhabitants of a place.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','residents of the building','residents to the building of','residence people buildinging','Of links the residents with their place.','grammar'),Q(1,'People who live in a neighborhood attend a local meeting. They are the…','residents','residuals','representatives necessarily','They are the people who live in that area.','context'),Q(1,'What is the singular form of residents?','resident','residential','reside','Resident is singular; residents is plural.','grammar')]);
P('residual','From residue + -al, from Latin residuum “that which remains”; residual means left after the main part or process has gone, or a leftover amount.',[C('residual.s1','通用','The technician wiped away residual glue after removing the label.','技师撕下标签后擦掉了残留的胶水。','residual heat/material/effects','形容词：主要部分被移除或过程完成后仍然留下的。','glue remains after removal.','通用'),C('residual.s2','科学','The formula includes a residual of two units after the division.','这个算式在除法后余下两个单位。','a residual amount/value','名词：处理或计算后剩下的数量。','calculation leaves two.','数学')],M('After the label was removed, no glue remained, yet the technician described the surface as covered in residual glue.','After the label was removed, a thin film of residual glue remained on the surface.','没有任何胶水残留时，不能说表面覆盖着 residual glue。','meaning'),[Q(1,'Residual glue is…','glue left after the label is removed','the label before it is peeled','a new layer added on purpose','Sense 1 describes what remains after removal.','meaning'),Q(2,'A residual of two units after division is…','the leftover amount','the original divisor','a resident of the equation','Sense 2 is a mathematical leftover.','context'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','residual effects of the storm','effects residualed by stormly','residually of storm the effects','Residual can modify effects that remain afterward.','grammar'),Q(1,'Residual is related to the noun…','residue','resident','resit','Residual describes a remainder or residue.','word-formation')]);
P('residue','From Latin residuum “that which remains,” from residere “remain”; residue is leftover matter after the main part is removed, or the remainder after use or payment.',[C('residue.s1','通用','A sticky residue remained on the jar after the paper label was peeled away.','纸质标签揭掉后，罐子上仍留有黏糊糊的残留物。','residue on/from + surface/material','名词：主体被移除后留下的物质或残渣。','adhesive remains on jar.','生活'),C('residue.s2','通用','The residue of the travel budget was returned to the department.','差旅预算中剩余的部分被退回了部门。','the residue of + amount/fund','名词：使用或付款后剩下的部分或余款。','unused funds returned.','商务')],M('After the adhesive was cleaned completely off the jar, a thick residue still covered the glass.','A small residue of adhesive remained on the jar after cleaning.','彻底清除后不可能还覆盖着厚厚残留物。','meaning'),[Q(1,'Sticky residue on a jar is…','matter left after the label is removed','a fresh label that has not been used','the jar’s reservation','Residue is leftover material.','meaning'),Q(2,'The residue of a travel budget is…','the part of the funds left after spending','the amount already spent in full','a rescheduled flight','Sense 2 is a remaining amount.','context'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','residue on the glass','residue into glassing','a residuary glass on','Residue can be followed by on to identify a surface.','grammar'),Q(1,'Residue means something that…','remains after the main part is gone','is newly produced for the first time','is formally requested','The word names what is left behind.','meaning')]);
P('resign','From Latin resignare “unseal, surrender,” from re- + signare “mark”; resign means formally leave a job or accept an unpleasant fact one cannot change.',[C('resign.s1','职场','The director resigned from her post after the board rejected her proposal.','董事会否决她的提案后，主任辞去了职务。','resign from + job/post; resign as + role','动词：正式声明离开职位或工作。','director leaves position.','职场'),C('resign.s2','书面','After several appeals failed, the family resigned themselves to the long wait.','几次申诉都失败后，这家人只好接受漫长等待的现实。','resign oneself to + situation','动词：接受无法改变的不愉快事实。','family accepts unavoidable delay.','书面')],M('The director resigned from her post by accepting a promotion and continuing in exactly the same role.','The director resigned from her post by formally announcing that she was leaving it.','继续留任不是辞职。','meaning'),[Q(1,'A director resigns from a post when she…','formally leaves the position','receives a promotion in the same position','reschedules the board meeting','Sense 1 means officially quit a job or office.','meaning'),Q(2,'They resigned themselves to a long wait. They…','accepted it as something they could not change','made the wait shorter by decree','reproduced the wait','Sense 2 means accept an unpleasant situation.','context'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','resign from the committee','resign to the committee from of','resign the committee out from','Resign from identifies the position being left.','grammar'),Q(1,'Which sentence uses resign in the “accept” sense?','She resigned herself to the delay.','She resigned as treasurer.','She signed the new contract.','Resign oneself to a situation means accept it.','meaning')]);
P('resignation','From resign + -ation, from Latin resignare “surrender”; resignation is a formal act or statement of leaving a post, or patient acceptance of an unpleasant situation.',[C('resignation.s1','职场','The chair submitted her resignation after the committee voted to replace her.','委员会投票决定更换主席后，她提交了辞呈。','submit/announce a resignation; resignation from + post','名词：正式离开职位的行为或书面辞呈。','chair leaves office.','职场'),C('resignation.s2','态度','He waited with resignation when the storm delayed the ferry for another day.','渡轮因风暴又延误一天时，他无奈地等待着。','accept/wait with resignation','名词：平静地接受无法改变的不愉快处境。','person accepts delay.','态度')],M('She submitted her resignation while insisting she had no intention of leaving her post.','She submitted her resignation and announced that she was leaving her post.','辞呈表示离开职位的意图，与坚称不打算离开相矛盾。','meaning'),[Q(1,'A written resignation is…','a formal statement that someone is leaving a post','a request to be promoted','a report about a reservoir','Sense 1 is a formal notice of departure.','meaning'),Q(2,'Waiting with resignation suggests…','patient acceptance of a situation one cannot change','lively excitement about a delay','a refusal to accept reality','Sense 2 is calm acceptance.','context'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','submit her resignation','submit her resign from','resignationing her position','One submits a resignation when leaving a post.','collocation'),Q(1,'Resignation is the noun formed from…','resign','resident','resin','It is formed from the verb resign with -ation.','word-formation')]);
P('resilience','From resilient + -ence, from Latin resilire “leap back”; resilience is the ability to recover quickly from hardship or for a material to return to shape after bending.',[C('resilience.s1','通用','The town showed resilience by restoring its schools and reopening shops after the flood.','洪水过后，这座小镇修复学校、重开商店，展现出复原力。','resilience after/from + hardship','名词：遭受损害或困难后迅速恢复的能力。','community recovers.','通用'),C('resilience.s2','通用','The rubber’s resilience lets it return to its original shape after being stretched.','这种橡胶的弹性使它拉伸后能恢复原状。','the resilience of + material','名词：材料弯曲或拉伸后恢复原形的能力。','material springs back.','材料')],M('The rubber’s resilience was demonstrated when it remained permanently stretched after a slight pull.','The rubber’s resilience was demonstrated when it returned to shape after being stretched.','永久变形说明材料没有恢复形状的弹性。','meaning'),[Q(1,'A town’s resilience after a flood is its ability to…','recover from hardship','avoid every challenge forever','reschedule the flood','Sense 1 concerns recovery from difficulty.','meaning'),Q(2,'A resilient rubber has high resilience because it…','returns to its shape after stretching','stays stretched permanently','is a resident of the factory','Sense 2 is a material’s spring-back property.','context'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','resilience in the face of hardship','resilience by hardship in the face to','resiliently of hardship','The phrase describes recovery despite hardship.','grammar'),Q(1,'Resilience is closely related to the adjective…','resilient','residential','requisite','Resilience names the quality of being resilient.','word-formation')]);
P('resilient','From Latin resilire “leap back,” with adjective suffix -ent; resilient means able to return to shape or recover quickly from stress and difficulty.',C('resilient.s1','通用','The resilient community rebuilt its clinic after the storm damaged the building.','风暴损坏诊所后，这个有韧性的社区把它重建起来。','a resilient person/community/material','形容词：受损或受压后能够复原的。','community recovers from setback.','通用'),M('The resilient foam remained crushed and could not return to its original shape after pressure was removed.','The resilient foam returned to its original shape after pressure was removed.','无法恢复形状的泡沫不具有弹性。','meaning'),[Q(1,'A resilient community…','recovers from hardship','is permanently defeated by every setback','requires a reservation','Resilient means able to recover after difficulty.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','a resilient material','a resilience materialed','resiliently material of','Resilient is an adjective modifying material.','grammar'),Q(1,'A rubber ball springs back after being compressed. It is…','resilient','residual','repressive','It returns to its shape after pressure.','context'),Q(1,'Which noun is formed from resilient?','resilience','resin','residence','Resilience is the noun for the quality of being resilient.','word-formation')]);
P('resin','From Latin resina, from Greek rhētinē “pine resin”; resin is a sticky solid substance produced by some trees and used in plastics, varnish, and other materials.',C('resin.s1','工业','The craft worker sealed the wooden bowl with a thin coat of clear resin.','手工艺者在木碗上涂了一层透明树脂作为封层。','pine/synthetic resin; coat/seal with resin','名词：某些树木产生的黏性固体，也可用于制造塑料和清漆。','resin coats wood.','工业'),M('The worker used resin to seal the bowl, but the material dissolved instantly and left no sticky solid coating.','The worker used resin to seal the bowl with a durable solid coating.','不能形成固体涂层、立刻溶解的物质不符合该词义。','meaning'),[Q(1,'Resin is…','a sticky solid substance from some trees or made synthetically','a liquid request for a seat','a reptile’s skin','Resin is a material used in varnish and plastics.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','seal the wood with resin','resin the wood at to sealing','seal the resin from the wood with out','Resin can be the material used to coat or seal wood.','grammar'),Q(1,'A craftsperson coats a bowl with a sticky substance that hardens. The substance may be…','resin','resignation','residence','Resin is used in coatings and manufactured materials.','context'),Q(1,'Pine resin is produced by…','some trees','republican governments','a research questionnaire','The word traditionally refers to a sticky tree substance.','meaning')]);
P('resist','From Latin resistere “stand firm against,” from re- + sistere “stand”; resist means fight an attack, refuse a change or force, or stop oneself from doing something attractive.',[C('resist.s1','通用','The volunteers resisted the attackers until help arrived.','志愿者们抵抗袭击者，直到援助赶到。','resist an attack/enemy','动词：与攻击或敌人对抗。','people defend themselves.','通用'),C('resist.s2','通用','The neighborhood resisted the plan to remove its only public garden.','社区抵制了拆除唯一公共花园的计划。','resist a change/pressure/plan','动词：拒绝接受某种变化或压力。','community opposes plan.','通用'),C('resist.s3','口语','I could not resist ordering the warm apple pie.','我忍不住点了热苹果派。','resist doing something; cannot resist','动词：克制自己不去做有吸引力的事。','temptation overcomes restraint.','口语')],M('The neighborhood resisted the plan by approving it unanimously and helping carry it out.','The neighborhood resisted the plan by opposing it at the public meeting.','一致批准并协助执行计划与抵制相反。','meaning'),[Q(1,'Volunteers resist an attack when they…','fight against it','welcome the attackers','reproduce the attack as a painting','Sense 1 means oppose an assault.','meaning'),Q(2,'A neighborhood resists a plan when it…','refuses to accept or support it','requires the plan by law','reschedules the meeting','Sense 2 concerns opposition to a change or proposal.','context'),Q(3,'“I could not resist ordering pie” means…','I could not stop myself from ordering it','I refused to order any food','I fought an attacker over it','Sense 3 means fail to control a temptation.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which pattern is grammatical?','resist buying another dessert','resist to buy another dessert','resist for buying another dessert','Resist can take a gerund as its object.','grammar')]);
P('resistance','From resist + -ance, from Latin resistere “stand firm against”; resistance is opposition to something or a force/quality that slows or prevents movement or change.',[C('resistance.s1','政治','Public resistance to the new toll delayed the road project.','公众对新收费制度的抵制使道路项目延期。','resistance to + change/authority','名词：反对某事或拒绝接受某项变化。','people oppose policy.','政治'),C('resistance.s2','科学','The thick coating gives the cable resistance to heat and moisture.','厚涂层使电缆能够抵抗热和潮气。','resistance to + force/condition','名词：减慢过程或使物体不易受影响的力或性质。','coating blocks damage.','科学')],M('The coating gave the cable resistance to moisture by making it absorb water more quickly.','The coating gave the cable resistance to moisture by preventing water from entering.','让电缆更快吸水会降低防潮能力。','meaning'),[Q(1,'Resistance to a toll means…','opposition to the new charge','agreement to pay every toll happily','a reprint of the road map','Sense 1 is opposition to a policy.','meaning'),Q(2,'A coating gives a cable resistance to moisture if it…','helps prevent water damage','makes water enter more easily','reschedules the cable','Sense 2 is a quality that protects against a force or condition.','context'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','resistance to change','resistance for changing to at','resistantness change by','Resistance is commonly followed by to.','grammar'),Q(1,'Resistance can refer to…','opposition or a force that slows something','a required place to live','an official resignation','Both source senses concern opposing or slowing something.','meaning')]);
P('resistant','From resist + -ant, from Latin resistere “stand firm against”; resistant means able to remain unaffected by a disease, chemical, pressure, or other force.',C('resistant.s1','健康','The resistant strain of bacteria survived the first antibiotic treatment.','这种耐药菌株在第一次抗生素治疗后存活了下来。','resistant to + disease/chemical/pressure','形容词：能够抵抗某种疾病、化学物质或压力而不受影响的。','strain withstands drug.','健康'),M('The coating was resistant to water, yet it absorbed every drop immediately and offered no protection.','The coating was resistant to water and kept the surface dry.','立即吸水说明它不防水、不具抵抗力。','meaning'),[Q(1,'Antibiotic-resistant bacteria…','can survive exposure to that antibiotic','are always killed by it immediately','reside inside an antibiotic','Resistant means able to withstand a substance.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','resistant to heat','resistant with heat at','resistance heatable','Resistant is followed by to before the condition resisted.','grammar'),Q(1,'A waterproof fabric keeps rain from soaking through. It is…','resistant to water','residual to water','repressive of water','It remains unaffected by exposure to water.','context'),Q(1,'Which verb is the base of resistant?','resist','reside','resell','Resistant is formed from resist + -ant.','word-formation')]);
P('resit','From re- “again” + sit, in the sense “sit an examination”; resit means take an exam again, usually after failing it the first time.',C('resit.s1','教育','After missing the pass mark, Leo plans to resit the biology exam in June.','没达到及格线后，利奥计划六月重考生物。','resit an exam/test; resit for + qualification','动词：通常在第一次未通过后再参加一次考试。','student takes exam again.','教育'),M('Leo resat the exam after passing it with the highest score and having no reason to take it again.','Leo resat the exam after failing to reach the pass mark.','第一次以最高分通过，与因未通过而重考的情景不符。','meaning'),[Q(1,'A student resits an exam because the student…','takes it again, usually after failing','takes it for the first time','resigns from school','Resit means sit an examination again.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','resit the mathematics exam','resit to the mathematics exam','resit the exam at first time only','Resit takes the exam as its direct object.','grammar'),Q(1,'Maya fails a test and registers for another attempt. She will…','resit the test','reside the test','resell the test','She is taking the examination again.','context'),Q(1,'What does re- mean in resit?','again','against','below','The candidate sits the exam a second time.','word-formation')]);
P('resolute','From Latin resolutus, past participle of resolvere “loosen, decide”; resolute means firmly determined and unlikely to give up, especially when facing difficulty.',C('resolute.s1','性格','Despite the delays, the resolute team continued repairing the bridge through the winter.','尽管工程延误，这支坚决的队伍仍整个冬天都在继续修桥。','a resolute decision/effort/person','形容词：态度坚定，遇到困难也不轻易放弃。','team persists.','性格'),M('The resolute team abandoned the repair at the first small setback and refused to continue.','The resolute team persisted with the repair despite setbacks.','遇到小挫折就放弃并非坚定不移。','meaning'),[Q(1,'A resolute team is…','firmly determined not to give up','uncertain and ready to quit','a group of residents','Resolute means determined and firm.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','a resolute effort to finish','a resolve effortly to finishing','resolute of an effort at','Resolute can describe a determined effort.','grammar'),Q(1,'A campaign continues despite repeated obstacles. Its organizers are…','resolute','residual','repressive','They remain determined while facing difficulty.','context'),Q(1,'Which word is closest to resolute?','determined','hesitant','reluctant','A resolute person is firmly determined.','meaning')]);
P('resolution','From Latin resolutio “a loosening, solution,” from resolvere; resolution is firm determination, an official decision, or the level of detail in an image.',[C('resolution.s1','心理','Her New Year’s resolution was to walk to work twice a week.','她的新年决心是每周步行上班两次。','make/keep a resolution to + verb','名词：决定要做或完成某事的坚定决心。','person makes a firm goal.','心理'),C('resolution.s2','政治','The council passed a resolution supporting the river cleanup.','委员会通过了一项支持河流清理工作的决议。','pass/adopt a resolution','名词：会议或组织正式作出的决定。','council votes.','政治'),C('resolution.s3','媒体','The monitor’s high resolution makes small text easier to read.','显示器的高分辨率让小字更容易辨认。','high/low image resolution','名词：图像细节的清晰程度，常由像素数衡量。','screen displays fine details.','媒体')],M('The council passed a resolution, but the motion was never voted on and no official decision was made.','The council passed a resolution after voting to support the cleanup.','未经表决或决定就不能说会议通过了决议。','meaning'),[Q(1,'A resolution to walk to work is…','a firm decision to do it','the pixel count of a monitor','a request for a new route','Sense 1 is a personal determination.','meaning'),Q(2,'A council resolution is…','an official decision made by the group','a private feeling of doubt','a resident’s home','Sense 2 is a formal collective decision.','context'),Q(3,'High image resolution means…','the image shows a high level of detail','the image has no pixels','the decision is final','Sense 3 concerns picture detail.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','pass a resolution','pass a resolving on','resolution a pass to','A council can pass or adopt a resolution.','collocation')]);
P('resolve','From Latin resolvere “loosen, solve,” from re- + solvere “loosen”; resolve means settle a problem, decide firmly to act, or a firm decision or formal vote.',[C('resolve.s1','通用','The mediator helped the neighbors resolve their disagreement over the shared fence.','调解员帮助邻居解决了他们对共用围栏的争议。','resolve a problem/dispute','动词：找到问题、分歧或争端的解决办法。','disagreement is settled.','通用'),C('resolve.s2','书面','After reviewing the risks, she resolved to report the damaged equipment.','审查风险后，她决定报告设备损坏一事。','resolve to do something','动词：坚定地决定要做某事。','person makes firm decision.','书面'),C('resolve.s3','书面','The board’s resolve to protect the wetland did not change during the debate.','董事会保护湿地的决心在辩论期间始终没有动摇。','show/maintain one’s resolve; a resolve to + verb','名词：坚定的决心，也可指团体的正式决议。','determination remains.','书面')],M('The mediator resolved the dispute by making the neighbors’ disagreement more severe and leaving it unsettled.','The mediator resolved the dispute by helping both neighbors agree on a fence repair.','加剧并保留争端没有解决问题。','meaning'),[Q(1,'To resolve a disagreement is to…','find a way to settle it','make it worse without agreement','reproduce it as an image','Sense 1 means settle a problem or dispute.','meaning'),Q(2,'She resolved to report the damage means she…','decided firmly that she would report it','was unsure whether to mention it','asked for a reservation','Sense 2 is a firm decision to act.','context'),Q(3,'The board showed resolve to protect the wetland. It showed…','firm determination','a pixel measurement','a request to reschedule','Resolve as a noun means determination.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which construction is correct?','resolve to report the problem','resolve for report the problem','resolve the problem to reporting it','Resolve to do something expresses a firm decision.','grammar')]);
P('resolved','From resolve + -ed; resolve is from Latin resolvere “solve, decide.” Resolved means firmly determined to carry out a decision.',C('resolved.s1','态度','After hearing the evidence, the committee was resolved to publish the safety findings.','听取证据后，委员会下定决心公布安全调查结果。','be resolved to + verb','形容词：已作出坚定决定并打算坚持执行。','committee commits to publication.','态度'),M('The resolved committee changed its mind every hour and never intended to carry out its decision.','The resolved committee remained committed to publishing the findings.','反复改变主意、毫无执行意图与坚定决心相反。','meaning'),[Q(1,'A resolved committee is…','firmly determined to act','unable to make any decision','a collection of residents','Resolved describes a firm commitment.','meaning'),Q(1,'Which phrase is grammatical?','resolved to publish the findings','resolved for publish findings','resolved publishing of to findings','Resolved is commonly followed by to + verb.','grammar'),Q(1,'After discussion, a board commits to finishing the project despite costs. It is…','resolved','residential','requisite','The board has made and intends to keep a firm decision.','context'),Q(1,'Resolved is based on which verb?','resolve','reside','resist','It is the -ed form of resolve used as an adjective.','word-formation')]);
P('resonance','From Latin resonantia “echo,” from resonare “sound again”; resonance is a deep ringing sound that continues, or a quality that evokes a strong emotional response.',[C('resonance.s1','科学','The chamber amplified the resonance of the low note after the singer stopped.','歌手停止发声后，房间仍放大了低音的共鸣。','resonance of + sound; acoustic resonance','名词：原声停止后仍持续的响亮回声或共振。','sound continues in chamber.','科学'),C('resonance.s1','通用','The story has lasting resonance for readers who have faced a similar loss.','这则故事能让经历过类似失去的读者久久产生共鸣。','emotional/cultural resonance; resonance for + audience','名词：能深深触动人或引发联想的特质。','readers feel story deeply.','通用')],M('The story had resonance for the audience, but it produced no response, association, or emotional effect whatsoever.','The story had resonance for the audience because it deeply reminded them of their own experiences.','完全没有引发回应或联想不符合引起共鸣的含义。','meaning'),[Q(1,'Acoustic resonance is…','a ringing or vibrating sound that continues','a request for an appointment','a resident’s official address','Sense 1 concerns sound and vibration.','meaning'),Q(1,'A story has resonance for readers when it…','touches them deeply or evokes associations','has no effect on anyone','is rescheduled for a new date','Sense 2 is emotional or cultural impact.','context'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','the resonance of the bell','the resonant of bell sound','resonance into the bellly','Resonance of the bell names the sound quality.','grammar'),Q(1,'The source verb resonare meant…','sound again','live permanently','sell another time','Resonance is connected to Latin for echoing or sounding again.','word-formation')]);
P('resonant','From resonance + -ant, from Latin resonare “sound again”; resonant means producing a deep continuing sound or suggesting strong meanings and feelings.',[C('resonant.s1','声音','The resonant bell could be heard across the valley long after it was struck.','这口洪亮的钟被敲响后，声音久久回荡在山谷间。','a resonant voice/note/bell','形容词：声音低沉清晰、洪亮并持续回响的；也可指产生共振的。','sound carries and lingers.','声音'),C('resonant.s2','文学','The closing image of the empty lighthouse is especially resonant in the novel.','小说结尾那幅空灯塔的意象尤其意味深长。','a resonant image/phrase/theme','形容词：能引发超出字面意义的联想或感受的。','image evokes extra meanings.','文学')],M('The resonant bell made no sound that could be heard beyond the hand holding it.','The resonant bell produced a deep ringing sound that carried across the valley.','声音无法传播、几乎听不见，不符合 resonant 的洪亮回响义。','meaning'),[Q(1,'A resonant bell…','produces a deep, continuing sound','is silent and cannot vibrate','is a formal request','Sense 1 describes ringing sound.','meaning'),Q(2,'A resonant image in a novel…','suggests feelings or ideas beyond its plain meaning','has no effect on readers','is a high-resolution photograph only','Sense 2 is rich with associations.','context'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','a resonant voice','a resonance voiceful','a voice resonanting of','Resonant is an adjective modifying voice.','grammar'),Q(1,'Resonant is closely related to the noun…','resonance','residence','resignation','A resonant sound has resonance.','word-formation')]);
})();
